tick: 406
role: model
parts:
- text: "Excellent. The baseline experiment has completed successfully. I now have a reliable benchmark score of **22.70** for the `DefaultResidualCNN`. This officially concludes step 4a of the Stagnation Protocol.\n\nNow I will proceed with step 4b: testing my three novel hypotheses. I will test them one at a time to ensure the results are clear and unambiguous. I will start with my first hypothesis: **Input Augmentation with Relational Features.**\n\nI will now write the code to implement the pushability masks and agent-box proximity channels and submit the experiment. The logic for generating these features will be placed within a custom `training_step` function, as it needs to modify the observations before they are passed to the network.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol 4b.1: Input Augmentation (Pushability Masks)\"\ntags: \"input augmentation, feature engineering, cnn, stagnation protocol\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first of three experiments testing\
    \ novel ideas under the Stagnation Protocol. This submission tests the hypothesis that augmenting the input with explicit relational features will improve performance. Specifically, I add 5 new channels to the observation tensor: 4 for directional 'pushability' of boxes and 1 for agent-box proximity.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n  # Use default network and optimizer\n  from system.defaults import default_create_network, default_create_optimizer, default_define_hyperparameters\n\n  # --- Custom Logic for Input Augmentation ---\n  def _augment_observation(obs: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"Adds 5 new channels to the observation tensor with relational features.\"\"\"\n      # Unpack one-hot encoded channels\n      empty, wall, target, agent, box, agent_target, box_target = [obs[:, :, i] for i in range(7)]\n\n      # Agent and box locations\n  \
    \    agent_pos = agent + agent_target\n      box_pos = box + box_target\n\n      # Padded versions for easy convolution-like operations\n      agent_padded = jnp.pad(agent_pos, 1, 'constant')\n      box_padded = jnp.pad(box_pos, 1, 'constant')\n      free_space_padded = jnp.pad(1 - (wall + box_pos), 1, 'constant') # Free space is not a wall or a box\n\n      # Proximity Masks\n      # Check if agent is adjacent to a box\n      up_prox = agent_padded[2:, 1:-1] * box_padded[1:-1, 1:-1]\n      down_prox = agent_padded[:-2, 1:-1] * box_padded[1:-1, 1:-1]\n      left_prox = agent_padded[1:-1, 2:] * box_padded[1:-1, 1:-1]\n      right_prox = agent_padded[1:-1, :-2] * box_padded[1:-1, 1:-1]\n      agent_box_proximity = up_prox + down_prox + left_prox + right_prox\n\n      # Pushability Masks\n      # Box is pushable if agent is on one side and the other side is free\n      pushable_up = agent_padded[2:, 1:-1] * box_padded[1:-1, 1:-1] * free_space_padded[:-2, 1:-1]\n      pushable_down = agent_padded[:-2,\
    \ 1:-1] * box_padded[1:-1, 1:-1] * free_space_padded[2:, 1:-1]\n      pushable_left = agent_padded[1:-1, 2:] * box_padded[1:-1, 1:-1] * free_space_padded[1:-1, :-2]\n      pushable_right = agent_padded[1:-1, :-2] * box_padded[1:-1, 1:-1] * free_space_padded[1:-1, 2:]\n\n      # Stack new features\n      new_features = jnp.stack([\n          pushable_up,\n          pushable_right, # Actions: 0: up, 1: right, 2: down, 3: left\n          pushable_down,\n          pushable_left,\n          agent_box_proximity\n      ], axis=-1)\n\n      # Concatenate with original observation\n      return jnp.concatenate([obs, new_features], axis=-1)\n\n  # --- Overridden Network Creation ---\n  # The network needs to accept a different input shape\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Creates the default CNN but modified for 13 input channels.\"\"\"\n      class AugmentedCNN(nn.Module):\n          cnn_features_1: int\n          cnn_features_2: int\n\n          @nn.compact\n     \
    \     def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state=None):\n              # We expect x to have shape (B, 8, 8, 13)\n              # The default network's logic is fine from here\n              batch_size = x.shape[0]\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              conv2_in = x\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = x + conv2_in\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              conv4_in = x\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = x + conv4_in\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n              x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n              policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n              policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n              value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n              value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n              value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n              return policy_logits, value, None\n\n      return AugmentedCNN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  # --- Overridden Training Step ---\n  # We need to augment the observations before they are used.\n  from system.defaults import default_training_step as original_training_step\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n\
    \      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \n      # Augment the observations in the batch\n      original_obs = batch['observations']\n      batch_size, trajectory_length = original_obs.shape[:2]\n      \n      # Vmap the augmentation function over the batch and trajectory dimensions\n      vmap_augment = vmap(vmap(_augment_observation))\n      augmented_obs = vmap_augment(original_obs)\n      \n      # Replace the original observations with the augmented ones\n      batch['observations'] = augmented_obs\n      \n      # Call the original default training step with the modified batch\n      return original_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n```"
