tick: 407
role: model
parts:
- text: "My first experiment (ID 693), testing input augmentation, is now running. As per the station rules, I can have two experiments running concurrently. To make efficient use of time, I will now submit my second experiment to test my second hypothesis: **Auxiliary State Prediction for Representation Learning.**\n\nThis experiment will modify the default CNN and training loop to include two auxiliary prediction heads. These heads will be trained to predict the number of boxes on target locations and the number of boxes off target locations. The goal is to force the network's shared layers to learn more meaningful representations of the game state, which should improve the main policy and value functions.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol 4b.2: Auxiliary State Prediction\"\ntags: \"auxiliary loss, representation learning, cnn, stagnation protocol\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second of three experiments testing novel ideas under the Stagnation Protocol.\
    \ This submission tests the hypothesis that adding auxiliary prediction tasks can improve representation learning. The default CNN is modified with two new output heads that predict the number of boxes on and off target locations. The loss from these heads is added to the main RL loss to encourage the learning of richer state features.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n  # Import GAE calculation from defaults\n  from system.defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  # --- Hyperparameter Definition ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameter search space, adding an auxiliary loss coefficient.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),\n          'aux_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.1]) # Coefficient for our new loss\n      }\n\n  # --- Custom Network with Auxiliary Heads ---\n  class AuxiliaryCNN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN with separated methods for backbone encoding and output heads.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state=None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, None]:\n          \"\"\"Main call for compatibility with the training script's validation.\"\"\"\n          features = self.encode(x)\n          policy_logits = self.decode_policy(features)\n          value = self.decode_value(features)\n          return policy_logits, value, None\n\n      def encode(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          \"\"\"Runs the CNN backbone to get shared features.\"\"\"\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          return nn.relu(x)\n\n      def decode_policy(self, features: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          \"\"\"Policy head.\"\"\"\n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(features)\n\
    \          policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          return nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n\n      def decode_value(self, features: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n          \"\"\"Value head.\"\"\"\n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(features)\n          value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n          return nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n\n      def decode_auxiliary(self, features: jnp.ndarray) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]:\n          \"\"\"Auxiliary heads for predicting box counts.\"\"\"\n          aux_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(features)\n          aux_hidden = nn.relu(aux_hidden)\n          pred_on_target = nn.Dense(features=1)(aux_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          pred_off_target = nn.Dense(features=1)(aux_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          return pred_on_target, pred_off_target\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Create and return the custom network.\"\"\"\n      return AuxiliaryCNN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  # --- Custom Training Step with Auxiliary Loss ---\n  def training_step(\n      network: AuxiliaryCNN,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \n      # Extract data and calculate GAE\n      observations, actions, rewards, dones = batch['observations'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones']\n      old_values, final_values = batch['values'], batch['final_values']\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      \n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n\n      # Ground truth for auxiliary tasks\n      # Channel 4 is 'box', Channel 6 is 'box_on_target'\n      true_off_target = jnp.sum(observations[:, :, :, :, 4], axis=(-1, -2))\n      true_on_target = jnp.sum(observations[:,\
    \ :, :, :, 6], axis=(-1, -2))\n\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          # Reshape for non-recurrent network\n          obs_reshaped = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n          \n          # Forward pass to get features and head outputs\n          features = network.apply(params, obs_reshaped, method=network.encode)\n          logits_flat = network.apply(params, features, method=network.decode_policy)\n          values_flat = network.apply(params, features, method=network.decode_value)\n          pred_on_target_flat, pred_off_target_flat = network.apply(params, features, method=network.decode_auxiliary)\n\n          # Reshape back\n          all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n          all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n          pred_on_target = pred_on_target_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n          pred_off_target = pred_off_target_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n\
    \          \n          # Policy Loss\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, actions[..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(advantages_detached * action_log_probs)\n          \n          # Value Loss\n          returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          \n          # Entropy Bonus\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          # Auxiliary Loss (MSE)\n          aux_loss_on_target = 0.5 * jnp.mean((pred_on_target - true_on_target) ** 2)\n          aux_loss_off_target = 0.5 * jnp.mean((pred_off_target - true_off_target) ** 2)\n          aux_loss = aux_loss_on_target + aux_loss_off_target\n          \n      \
    \    # Total Loss\n          total_loss = (policy_loss + \n                        hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - \n                        hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy +\n                        hparams['aux_loss_coef'] * aux_loss)\n          return total_loss\n\n      # Calculate gradients and update\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      \n      return params, opt_state\n\n  # Use the default optimizer creator\n  from system.defaults import default_create_optimizer\n```"
thinking_content: '**Stagnation Protocol 4b.2: Auxiliary State Prediction**


  Okay, so experiment 693 is running, but I''m going to be proactive here and get the next one prepped.  I''m going to start working on the second hypothesis, "Auxiliary State Prediction" - this should increase the network''s understanding of the environment and help with training.  Since I''m allowed to have two experiments running at the same time, it makes sense to start setting this up.


  First, I need to design the network architecture. This is where it gets interesting. I''ll inherit from the base CNN but add two new output heads, which will predict the number of boxes on target and off target. It''s a regression task, so I''ll be using MSE loss.


  Next, I need to modify the `training_step`.  The main change will be including the auxiliary heads and their MSE loss contribution to the total loss. I''ll also add a new hyperparameter, `aux_loss_coef`, to control the weight of this auxiliary loss. I''ll keep the value fixed for now. I''ll also need to calculate the target values for these auxiliary tasks from the observations.


  Here''s the tricky part, though.  I''m constrained by the system; the network has to return two or three outputs, and I need a way to integrate my auxiliary predictions in a clean way.  The simplest solution is to redefine the whole network and `training_step`. The network will have separate methods for encoding and decoding, and the `__call__` will only return the standard outputs that the system expects. This keeps me compliant while allowing me to add the auxiliary tasks in the loss function.


  I''ll start by defining the new `AuxiliaryCNN`, with explicit policy, value, and auxiliary heads, and the `encode` and `decode` methods. Then, inside the new `training_step`, I will call the network''s `encode` and then the three decoders, compute the losses, and update the weights.


  I think this method should work. Now let''s implement the code, write the submission title, tags, and abstract, and get this second experiment running!

  '
