tick: 410
role: model
parts:
- text: "Both of my fixed submissions (ID 697 and 699) have failed again. This time, the error is different and more subtle: `Evaluation failed: No trial files found`. The STDOUT shows that the Ray Tune optimization started, but it seems no results were produced. The STDERR log is filled with repeated `Gym` warnings but no obvious fatal error. This suggests a silent failure within the Ray training workers, possibly due to a logical error in my code that only manifests during the JIT-compiled training loop.\n\nI need to debug this. I will focus on getting just one experiment working first: the \"Input Augmentation\" submission (ID 697). The error is likely in the new code I introduced. A possible culprit is my `_augment_observation` function. JAX's JIT compiler can be sensitive to array indexing and shapes. My manual padding and slicing might be causing an issue that the initial CPU validation doesn't catch.\n\nTo debug, I will simplify my `_augment_observation` function dramatically. I will\
    \ have it create the new channels but fill them with zeros. If this version runs, it confirms that the overall structure (adding channels, modifying the network, custom training step) is correct, and the problem lies specifically in the feature calculation logic. This is a standard debugging technique: reduce the problem to the simplest possible case to isolate the fault.\n\nI will now submit this simplified test version.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol 4b.1-debug: Input Augmentation (Zeroed Channels)\"\ntags: \"debug, input augmentation, cnn, stagnation protocol\"\nabstract: |\n  Debugging submission for ID 697. Both previous attempts failed silently during Ray Tune training. This version tests if the issue lies in the feature calculation logic by replacing the complex observation augmentation with simple zero-filled channels. If this runs, it isolates the bug to the content of the _augment_observation function.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import\
    \ jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import vmap, jit, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n  # --- COPIED FROM system/defaults.py ---\n  def default_define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def default_create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n  \n  @jit\n  def default_calculate_gae(rewards, values, dones, gamma=0.97, gae_lambda=0.97, next_values=None):\n      assert next_values is not None\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma\
    \ * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      \n      def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n          advantage_t = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * advantage_t_plus_1\n          return advantage_t, advantage_t\n      \n      _, advantages = lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1))\n      return advantages[::-1].T\n\n  def original_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      observations, actions, rewards, dones = batch['observations'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones']\n      old_values, final_values = batch['values'], batch['final_values']\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          obs_reshaped = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n\
    \          dones_reshaped = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n          logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_reshaped, dones_reshaped)\n          all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n          all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          action_log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, actions[..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(advantages_detached * action_log_probs)\n          returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1), axis=-1))\n          total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss\
    \ - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n          return total_loss\n      \n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n  # --- END COPIED SECTION ---\n\n  # --- DEBUG: SIMPLIFIED Augmentation Logic ---\n  def _augment_observation(obs: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"DEBUG VERSION: Adds 5 zero-filled channels.\"\"\"\n      zero_features = jnp.zeros(obs.shape[:2] + (5,))\n      return jnp.concatenate([obs, zero_features], axis=-1)\n\n  # --- Overridden Network Creation ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      class AugmentedCNN(nn.Module):\n          cnn_features_1: int\n          cnn_features_2: int\n          @nn.compact\n          def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state=None):\n              batch_size = x.shape[0]\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3,\
    \ 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x_res = x\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = x + x_res; x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x_res = x\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = x + x_res; x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n              x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n              policy_h = nn.Dense(features=64)(x); policy_h = nn.relu(policy_h)\n              policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_h)\n\
    \              value_h = nn.Dense(features=64)(x); value_h = nn.relu(value_h)\n              value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_h).squeeze(-1)\n              return policy_logits, value, None\n      return AugmentedCNN(cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'])\n\n  # --- Overridden Training Step ---\n  def training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      original_obs = batch['observations']\n      vmap_augment = vmap(vmap(_augment_observation))\n      augmented_obs = vmap_augment(original_obs)\n      batch['observations'] = augmented_obs\n      return original_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams)\n\n  # Expose functions to the submission runner\n  _define_hyperparameters = default_define_hyperparameters\n  create_optimizer = default_create_optimizer\n```"
