tick: 413
role: model
parts:
- text: "Success! My debugging experiment (ID 705) has completed with a score of **25.0**. This is a major breakthrough. It confirms two critical things:\n\n1.  The structural hypothesis was correct: the silent failures were caused by wrapping the `training_step`. Encapsulating custom logic within the network's `__call__` method and using the default `training_step` is the correct, robust approach.\n2.  Even with zero-filled channels (providing no actual information), the score (25.0) is slightly *higher* than the baseline (22.7). This is likely noise, but it's an encouraging sign that the larger network created by adding channels is not inherently detrimental.\n\nNow that I have a stable, working structure, I can finally test my first hypothesis properly. I will resubmit the \"Input Augmentation\" experiment, but this time with the *actual* feature calculation logic implemented inside the network's `__call__` method.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol 4b.1-final:\
    \ In-Network Input Augmentation\"\ntags: \"input augmentation, feature engineering, cnn, stagnation protocol\"\nabstract: |\n  Final version of the Input Augmentation experiment. After debugging the submission structure, this version implements the full relational feature logic (pushability masks, etc.) directly within the network's __call__ method, using the now-validated robust submission pattern. This will provide a clean test of the core hypothesis.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # This submission uses the default training_step.\n\n  # --- COPIED FROM system/defaults.py ---\n  def default_define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  def default_create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n  # --- END COPIED SECTION ---\n\n  # --- Custom Network with In-built Augmentation ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      class AugmentedCNN(nn.Module):\n          cnn_features_1: int\n          cnn_features_2: int\n\n          def _augment_observation(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n              \"\"\"Adds 5 new channels to the observation tensor with relational features.\"\"\"\n              # x shape is (B, H, W, C)\n              # Unpack one-hot encoded channels for the whole batch\n              empty, wall, _, agent, box, agent_target, box_target = [x[..., i] for i in range(7)]\n              \n              agent_pos = agent + agent_target\n              box_pos = box + box_target\n              \n              agent_padded = jnp.pad(agent_pos, ((0,0), (1,1), (1,1)), 'constant')\n\
    \              box_padded = jnp.pad(box_pos, ((0,0), (1,1), (1,1)), 'constant')\n              free_space_padded = jnp.pad(1 - (wall + box_pos), ((0,0), (1,1), (1,1)), 'constant')\n\n              # Proximity and Pushability Masks for the whole batch\n              up_prox = agent_padded[:, 2:, 1:-1] * box_padded[:, 1:-1, 1:-1]\n              down_prox = agent_padded[:, :-2, 1:-1] * box_padded[:, 1:-1, 1:-1]\n              left_prox = agent_padded[:, 1:-1, 2:] * box_padded[:, 1:-1, 1:-1]\n              right_prox = agent_padded[:, 1:-1, :-2] * box_padded[:, 1:-1, 1:-1]\n              agent_box_proximity = up_prox + down_prox + left_prox + right_prox\n              \n              pushable_up = up_prox * free_space_padded[:, :-2, 1:-1]\n              pushable_down = down_prox * free_space_padded[:, 2:, 1:-1]\n              pushable_left = left_prox * free_space_padded[:, 1:-1, :-2]\n              pushable_right = right_prox * free_space_padded[:, 1:-1, 2:]\n              \n          \
    \    new_features = jnp.stack([pushable_up, pushable_right, pushable_down, pushable_left, agent_box_proximity], axis=-1)\n              return jnp.concatenate([x, new_features], axis=-1)\n\n          @nn.compact\n          def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state=None):\n              x = self._augment_observation(x)\n              \n              batch_size = x.shape[0]\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x_res = x\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = x + x_res; x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x_res = x\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              x = x + x_res; x = nn.relu(x)\n              x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n              x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n              policy_h = nn.Dense(features=64)(x); policy_h = nn.relu(policy_h)\n              policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_h)\n              value_h = nn.Dense(features=64)(x); value_h = nn.relu(value_h)\n              value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_h).squeeze(-1)\n              return policy_logits, value, None\n\n      return AugmentedCNN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  # Expose functions to the submission runner\n  _define_hyperparameters = default_define_hyperparameters\n  create_optimizer = default_create_optimizer\n```"
