tick: 415
role: model
parts:
- text: "My second experiment (ID 715) is now running. While I wait for the results, I will use my second available experiment slot to test my third and final hypothesis: **Invalid Action Masking.**\n\nThis experiment will modify the network to mask out invalid actions from the policy's output logits before the softmax operation. This should prevent the agent from wasting learning capacity on impossible moves and focus its exploration on valid choices. I will use the validated in-network modification pattern to ensure the submission runs correctly.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol 4b.3-final: Invalid Action Masking\"\ntags: \"action masking, inductive bias, cnn, stagnation protocol\"\nabstract: |\n  Final experiment for the Stagnation Protocol. This submission tests the hypothesis that explicitly masking invalid actions (e.g., moving into a wall) will improve learning efficiency and performance. The logic is implemented within the network's __call__ method\
    \ to prevent the policy from assigning probability mass to impossible actions.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # This submission uses the default training_step.\n\n  # --- COPIED FROM system/defaults.py ---\n  def default_define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def default_create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n  # --- END COPIED SECTION ---\n\n  # --- Custom Network with Action Masking ---\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      class MaskedCNN(nn.Module):\n          cnn_features_1: int\n\
    \          cnn_features_2: int\n\n          def get_valid_actions_mask(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n              \"\"\"Determines valid actions from the observation tensor.\"\"\"\n              # x shape: (B, H, W, C)\n              wall = x[..., 1]\n              agent = x[..., 3] + x[..., 5]\n              \n              # Find agent position (assuming one agent per grid)\n              agent_coords = jnp.argwhere(agent > 0, size=x.shape[0])\n              agent_y = agent_coords[:, 1]\n              agent_x = agent_coords[:, 2]\n\n              # Check adjacent cells for walls\n              # Padded wall for easier indexing\n              wall_padded = jnp.pad(wall, ((0,0), (1,1), (1,1)), 'constant', constant_values=1)\n              \n              # agent_y+1, agent_x+1 because of padding\n              # Action order: 0: up, 1: right, 2: down, 3: left\n              can_move_up = wall_padded[jnp.arange(x.shape[0]), agent_y, agent_x+1] == 0\n              can_move_right\
    \ = wall_padded[jnp.arange(x.shape[0]), agent_y+1, agent_x+2] == 0\n              can_move_down = wall_padded[jnp.arange(x.shape[0]), agent_y+2, agent_x+1] == 0\n              can_move_left = wall_padded[jnp.arange(x.shape[0]), agent_y+1, agent_x] == 0\n              \n              return jnp.stack([can_move_up, can_move_right, can_move_down, can_move_left], axis=-1)\n\n          @nn.compact\n          def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state=None):\n              valid_actions_mask = self.get_valid_actions_mask(x)\n              \n              # Standard CNN backbone\n              batch_size = x.shape[0]\n              features = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n              features = nn.relu(features)\n              res = features\n              features = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(features)\n              features = nn.relu(features)\n              features = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(features)\n              features = features + res; features = nn.relu(features)\n              features = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(features)\n              features = nn.relu(features)\n              res = features\n              features = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(features)\n              features = nn.relu(features)\n              features = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(features)\n              features = features + res; features = nn.relu(features)\n              features = features.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n              features = nn.Dense(features=256)(features); features = nn.relu(features)\n              \n              # Policy head\n              policy_h = nn.Dense(features=64)(features); policy_h = nn.relu(policy_h)\n              policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_h)\n             \
    \ \n              # Apply mask\n              policy_logits = jnp.where(valid_actions_mask, policy_logits, -1e9)\n              \n              # Value head\n              value_h = nn.Dense(features=64)(features); value_h = nn.relu(value_h)\n              value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_h).squeeze(-1)\n              \n              return policy_logits, value, None\n\n      return MaskedCNN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  # Expose functions to the submission runner\n  _define_hyperparameters = default_define_hyperparameters\n  create_optimizer = default_create_optimizer\n```"
