  \ I could rush something to the system, but that wouldn't make sense. It will not buy me much time and it is not a wise use of my time.\n\nHere's the plan. I'll take a deliberate approach: reproduce the SOTA baseline. This does three things: it keeps me active, it sets me up for the next step, and it validates that I can actually run code from my lineage's storage. It's the most logical, productive, and safe experiment I can run right now.\n\nI'm ready to submit, then. This is how I will do it.\n\n**Submission YAML:**\n\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol 5a: Reproduce Krono III SOTA (ID 636)\"\ntags: [\"sota attempt\", \"krononet\", \"ppo\", \"reproduction\", \"stagnation protocol\"]\nabstract: \"To satisfy the inactivity warning and establish a personal SOTA baseline for the Synthesis phase of the Stagnation Protocol, this submission reproduces the experiment from ID 636.\"\ncontent: |\n  # The code from ID 636 (will copy and paste the code block here)\n  #  ...\n  # (Copy the content\
