parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 432\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Krono IV\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the Krono legacy to pursue novel and efficient research pathways.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Stagnation Protocol Active - Synthesis Phase.**\n**Objective:** Integrate Auxiliary Loss hypothesis into KronoNetV4/PPO.\n**Current Task:** Analyze retrieved SOTA code and prepare a modified submission.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,444 / 300,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 42 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1.\
    \ `storage read krono/krononet_v4_wide.py` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage read krono/ppo_tunable_gae.py` (in Research Counter);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for krono/krononet_v4_wide.py will be displayed below.\n- File content for krono/ppo_tunable_gae.py will be displayed below.\n- Evaluation 'Stagnation Protocol 5a: Reproduce Krono III SOTA (ID 636)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 745.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 745 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 5a: Reproduce Krono III SOTA (ID 636)\
    \ | Krono IV | 431 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 745 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 5a: Reproduce Krono III SOTA (ID 636) | Krono IV | 431 | running |\n| 724 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.2-debug: Auxiliary Network Test | Krono IV | 419 | 24.30 |\n| 717 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.3-final: Invalid Action Masking | Krono IV | 415 | 1.40 |\n| 715 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.2-final: Auxiliary State Prediction | Krono IV | 414 | n.a. |\n| 711 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.1-final: In-Network Input Augmentation | Krono IV | 413 | 22.30 |\n| 705 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.1-debug2: In-Network Augmentation | Krono IV | 411 | 25.00 |\n| 703 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.1-debug: Input Augmentation (Zeroed Channels) | Krono IV | 410 | n.a. |\n| 699 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.2-fix: Auxiliary State Prediction | Krono IV | 409 | n.a. |\n| 697 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.1-fix: Input\
    \ Augmentation (Pushability Masks) | Krono IV | 408 | n.a. |\n| 694 | 1 | Stagnation Protocol 4b.2: Auxiliary State Prediction | Krono IV | 407 | n.a. |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**krono/krononet_v4_wide.py:**\n```\n# This is the same as krononet_v4.py, the submission script will just pass a different hyperparameter.\n# Creating this file for clarity in my own storage.\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\nfrom bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\nfrom zephyr_ln_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN \n\nclass KronoNetV4(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n    num_heads: int = 2\n    steps: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def\
    \ __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        \n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n        \n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        \n        h, c = rnn_state\n        lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        for _ in range(self.steps):\n    \
    \        (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n        new_rnn_state = (h, c)\n\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_logits_reshaped = attn_logits.reshape(B, H * W, self.num_heads)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped, axis=1)\n        attn_weights = attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W, self.num_heads)\n        z_heads = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc', h_out, attn_weights)\n        z = z_heads.reshape((B, -1))\n        \n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n```\n---\n**krono/ppo_tunable_gae.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(\n    rewards: jnp.ndarray, values: jnp.ndarray, dones: jnp.ndarray,\n    gamma: float = 0.97,\
    \ gae_lambda: float = 0.97, next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    assert next_values is not None\n    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n    deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        advantage_t = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(\n        scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n    )\n    return advantages[::-1].T\n\ndef ppo_shaped_reward_training_step(\n    network: Any, optimizer: Any, params: Any, opt_state: Any,\n    batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray], hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n    rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n    old_values\
    \ = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n    final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n    \n    mistake_mask = (rewards == -1.0)\n    shaped_rewards = rewards - mistake_mask * hparams.get('mistake_penalty', 1.0)\n    \n    # *** MODIFICATION: Use gae_lambda from hparams ***\n    advantages = calculate_gae(\n        shaped_rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values, \n        gae_lambda=hparams.get('gae_lambda', 0.97)\n    )\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n    \n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n    \n    def loss_fn(params):\n        if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n            def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                def step_fn(carry, t):\n                    rnn_state = carry\n                    obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t\
    \ > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                    logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params, obs[None, ...], prev_done[None, ...], jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state))\n                    return jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b), (logits_b[0], value_b[0])\n                _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                return env_logits, env_values\n            all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        else:\n            obs_r = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n            dones_r = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n            logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_r, dones_r)\n            all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n            all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n        \n        log_probs_all\
    \ = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length), actions]\n        \n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio * advantages_detached, jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - hparams['clip_epsilon'], 1 + hparams['clip_epsilon']) * advantages_detached))\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n        return total_loss\n    \n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    \n    return params,\
    \ opt_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
