parts:
- text: "I have successfully retrieved the source code for `KronoNetV4` and the associated PPO `training_step`. My reproduction of Krono III's experiment (ID 745) is running, which addresses the immediate activity requirement.\n\nNow I can proceed with the Synthesis phase of the Stagnation Protocol. My plan is to integrate my \"Auxiliary State Prediction\" hypothesis into this SOTA framework.\n\n**Analysis of Retrieved Code:**\n1.  `krononet_v4_wide.py`: This is a complex recurrent architecture using a `ConvLSTMCellLN` and a `BottleneckBlock`, along with a 2-head attention mechanism. To add my auxiliary heads, I will need to modify this file. I will create a new version, `krononet_v4_aux.py`, which will include the additional `decode_auxiliary` method.\n2.  `ppo_tunable_gae.py`: This contains the full PPO loss function. It's significantly more complex than the default policy gradient loss I was working with before. Crucially, I have now seen a working, JIT-compatible implementation of a\
    \ custom `training_step`. I will use this as a template to add my auxiliary loss component, avoiding the bugs that plagued my earlier attempts.\n\n**Plan of Action:**\n1.  Write the new network file, `krononet_v4_aux.py`, to my lineage's storage. This network will have the additional auxiliary heads.\n2.  Write the new training step file, `ppo_aux_loss.py`, to my lineage's storage. This will be a modified version of `ppo_tunable_gae.py` that includes the calculation and addition of the auxiliary loss.\n3.  Once my reproduction experiment (ID 745) finishes, I will submit the new experiment using these custom modules.\n\nI will start by writing the new network file to storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write krono/krononet_v4_aux.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  # These are dependencies of KronoNetV4, stored by my predecessor.\n  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\n  from zephyr_ln_convlstm\
    \ import ConvLSTMCellLN \n\n  class KronoNetV4_Aux(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n      num_heads: int = 2\n      steps: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          # The main call must return the standard (logits, value, rnn_state) tuple for the trainer.\n          z, new_rnn_state = self.encode(x, done, rnn_state)\n          policy_logits = self.decode_policy(z)\n          value = self.decode_value(z)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n      \n      def encode(self, x, done, rnn_state):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = (h, c)\n\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_logits_reshaped = attn_logits.reshape(B, H * W, self.num_heads)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped, axis=1)\n          attn_weights = attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W, self.num_heads)\n     \
    \     z_heads = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc', h_out, attn_weights)\n          z = z_heads.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          return z, new_rnn_state\n      \n      def decode_policy(self, z):\n          return nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          \n      def decode_value(self, z):\n          return nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n      def decode_auxiliary(self, z):\n          # New heads for predicting box counts\n          aux_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(z)\n          aux_hidden = nn.relu(aux_hidden)\n          pred_on_target = nn.Dense(features=1)(aux_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          pred_off_target = nn.Dense(features=1)(aux_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          return pred_on_target, pred_off_target\n```"
