tick: 446
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My latest attempt to test the Auxiliary Loss hypothesis (ID 770) has failed again with the same silent JIT compilation error.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThis is a significant setback. My corrected script, `ppo_aux_loss_v2.py`, which I believed had fixed the JIT issue by more closely emulating the working PPO implementation, has also failed. The bug is more deeply rooted and subtle than I anticipated. The complexity of modifying a recurrent PPO training loop while maintaining JIT compatibility is proving to be a major engineering obstacle.\n\nAt this point, continuing to debug this specific implementation is a low-yield strategy. I have spent many ticks on this single idea with no success. The core principle of the Stagnation Protocol and the reviewer feedback is to produce *rigorous, reproducible results*. My current path is failing to produce any results at all.\n\nTherefore, I am making a strategic decision to **abandon the Auxiliary Loss hypothesis**.\
    \ The implementation is too fragile, and I cannot afford to waste more time on it.\n\nI must pivot to a new, simpler idea that I can implement with high confidence. Reviewing Insight I's successful Stagnation Protocol paper (ID 28) provides a clear path forward. Their most successful idea was **ConvLSTM Input Normalization**, which yielded a +14.1% improvement on a simple baseline and a +0.7% improvement on a complex PPO baseline. This is a validated, promising idea.\n\nMy new research plan will be to replicate and extend Insight I's work on my lineage's SOTA baseline, KronoNetV4. This aligns with the station's collaborative spirit and focuses my efforts on a proven concept.\n\n**New Research Plan:**\n1.  **Replication:** Replicate Insight I's \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" on the KronoNetV4 baseline.\n2.  **Ablation/Extension:** If successful, I can explore variations, such as different normalization types (GroupNorm vs LayerNorm) or applying normalization at different points in the\
    \ network.\n\nI will begin by writing a new network file, `krononet_v4_inputnorm.py`, that incorporates Insight I's successful modification.\n\n/execute_action{storage write krono/krononet_v4_inputnorm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\n  from zephyr_ln_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN \n\n  class KronoNetV4_InputNorm(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n      num_heads: int = 2\n      steps: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # CNN Backbone\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out\
    \ = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # Insight I's successful modification: Add LayerNorm before the ConvLSTM\n          cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")(cnn_out)\n\n          # Recurrent Core\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = (h, c)\n\n          # Attention\
    \ Pooling and MLP Heads\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_logits_reshaped = attn_logits.reshape(B, H * W, self.num_heads)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped, axis=1)\n          attn_weights = attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W, self.num_heads)\n          z_heads = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc', h_out, attn_weights)\n          z = z_heads.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Research Pivot 2: Abandoned Auxiliary Loss.**\n  **Objective:** Replicate and extend Insight I's successful \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" finding on the KronoNetV4 baseline.\n  **Current Task:** Wrote new network script to storage. Next, submit the experiment.\n```"
