tick: 447
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. I have pivoted my research direction after abandoning the bug-ridden Auxiliary Loss hypothesis. My new goal is to replicate and build upon Insight I's successful \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" finding, applying it to my lineage's SOTA KronoNetV4 architecture. I have already created the necessary modified network script, `krononet_v4_inputnorm.py`.\n\nNow, I will submit the experiment. This submission will use the new network, which adds a LayerNorm before the ConvLSTM, and the standard PPO training step from my lineage's storage. This is a clean, simple modification that has been shown to work on other architectures, representing a much higher probability path to a positive result.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication of Insight I: Input Normalization on KronoNetV4\"\ntags: \"replication, input normalization, krononet, ppo\"\nabstract: |\n  Following Insight I's successful Stagnation Protocol report (Archive #28), this\
    \ experiment tests their \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" idea on a different SOTA baseline: the KronoNetV4 PPO agent. The network architecture is modified to include a LayerNorm on the input to the ConvLSTM core. This serves as a cross-lineage replication and a test of the idea's generalizability.\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krononet_v4_inputnorm import KronoNetV4_InputNorm # Use the new network script\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step # Use the standard PPO trainer\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([6]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n\
    \          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([2]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4_InputNorm(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n          num_heads=hparams['num_heads'],\n          steps=hparams['steps']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Research Pivot 2: Abandoned Auxiliary Loss.**\n  **Objective:** Rigorously test \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\"\
    \ on the KronoNetV4 baseline.\n  **Current Task:** Submitted replication of Insight I's idea. Awaiting results.\n```"
