tick: 451
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My ablation experiment (ID 784), comparing GroupNorm to LayerNorm, is currently running.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThis is a moment of significant progress. After a period of failure and re-evaluation, I have successfully identified a promising research direction, replicated the key finding, and am now systematically building upon it. This methodical, step-by-step approach, modeled after the successful papers in the Archive, feels much more robust and scientifically sound. The activity in the station is high, with agents like Zephyr II and Nomos III also testing new ideas. My work on replicating and extending Insight I's finding is a direct contribution to this collaborative effort to break the station's stagnation.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nWhile my ablation study is running, I will prepare for the next and final experimental step required for a strong paper: the generalization test. As per the reviewer feedback and best practices, I must test my finding\
    \ on a second, distinct architecture.\n\nThe `DefaultResidualCNN` baseline from my Stagnation Protocol experiments is the perfect candidate. It is simple, non-recurrent, and I have a reliable performance benchmark for it (ID 689, score 22.7). I will test if adding Input Normalization *before the MLP backbone* of this simple CNN provides any benefit. This will test whether the normalization principle applies only to recurrent models or more broadly.\n\nFirst, I need to create the new network script for this generalization test. I will name it `default_cnn_inputnorm.py`. Since the default CNN has no ConvLSTM, I will apply the LayerNorm to the flattened features just before they enter the main MLP.\n\nI will use my second experiment slot to prepare this file in my lineage's storage. I will *not* submit the experiment yet, as I want to see the result of the GroupNorm ablation first. This is an efficient use of my time while waiting.\n\n/execute_action{storage write krono/default_cnn_inputnorm.py}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Tuple\n\n  class DefaultCNN_InputNorm(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Default CNN with LayerNorm applied before the main MLP backbone.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state=None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, None]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # CNN Backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.relu(x)\n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten and APPLY LAYERNORM\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          x = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"mlp_input_layernorm\")(x)\n          \n          # Shared MLP backbone\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Policy and Value Heads\n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(policy_hidden)\n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(features=64)(x)\n          value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits,\
    \ value, None\n```"
