tick: 452
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. I have received the results of my GroupNorm ablation study (ID 784) and have successfully created the script for my generalization test.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe results from the ablation study are very informative.\n-   **Baseline (ID 745):** 90.2\n-   **LayerNorm (ID 776):** 92.8 (+2.6)\n-   **GroupNorm (ID 784):** 90.6 (+0.4)\n\nThis demonstrates that while normalizing the input to the ConvLSTM is generally beneficial, `LayerNorm` is significantly more effective than `GroupNorm` in this specific architectural context. This is a strong finding that deepens the understanding of the original idea and will be a key point in my future paper.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI have now completed the first three experiments of my new research arc. The final step is the generalization test. I have already prepared the script `default_cnn_inputnorm.py`. I will now submit the experiment to test whether applying LayerNorm to the flattened features before the MLP\
    \ of the simple `DefaultResidualCNN` provides any benefit. This will determine if the normalization effect is specific to recurrent architectures.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization Test: Input Normalization on Simple CNN\"\ntags: \"generalization, input normalization, cnn, layernorm\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the generalization test for the \"ConvLSTM Input Normalization\" research arc. Having shown that LayerNorm significantly improves the recurrent KronoNetV4 architecture, this experiment tests the same principle on a non-recurrent baseline: the DefaultResidualCNN. LayerNorm is applied to the flattened features before they enter the main MLP. The goal is to determine if the benefit of feature normalization is specific to recurrent networks.\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from default_cnn_inputnorm import DefaultCNN_InputNorm # Use the new CNN with LN script\n\n  # We need the default PG\
    \ trainer for this baseline\n  import jax; from jax import jit, lax; import flax.linen as nn\n\n  @jit\n  def default_calculate_gae(rewards, values, dones, gamma=0.97, gae_lambda=0.97, next_values=None):\n      assert next_values is not None\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(adv_t_p_1, t):\n          adv_t = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * adv_t_p_1\n          return adv_t, adv_t\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1))\n      return advantages[::-1].T\n\n  def default_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      obs, acts, rews, dones = batch['observations'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones']\n      old_vals, final_vals = batch['values'], batch['final_values']\n\
    \      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rews, old_vals, dones, next_values=final_vals)\n      returns = advantages + old_vals\n      B, T = obs.shape[:2]\n      \n      def loss_fn(params):\n          obs_r = obs.reshape(B*T, *obs.shape[2:]); dones_r = dones.reshape(B*T)\n          logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_r, dones_r)\n          logits, values = logits_flat.reshape(B,T,-1), values_flat.reshape(B,T)\n          log_probs_all = nn.log_softmax(logits, axis=-1)\n          log_probs = jnp.take_along_axis(log_probs_all, acts[..., None], axis=-1).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          adv_det = lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          pg_loss = -jnp.mean(adv_det * log_probs)\n          \n          ret_det = lax.stop_gradient(returns)\n          val_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((values - ret_det) ** 2)\n          \n          ent = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n          \n          total_loss = pg_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef']\
    \ * val_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * ent\n          return total_loss\n      \n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      return optax.apply_updates(params, updates), opt_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DefaultCNN_InputNorm(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  training_step = default_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Research Arc:\
    \ ConvLSTM Input Normalization.**\n  **Status:** Core hypothesis confirmed (92.8). Ablation confirmed LN > GN (90.6).\n  **Current Task:** Submitted Generalization Test on simple CNN. Awaiting results to complete the study.\n```"
