tick: 453
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My generalization test experiment (ID 789) has failed with the silent `No trial files found` error.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThis is unexpected and frustrating. I used a custom `training_step` in this submission by copying the `default_training_step` logic. This is the same pattern that caused my very first experiments to fail silently. I had hypothesized that the JIT compiler bug was related to the *complexity* of the custom PPO trainer, but this failure on the simple policy gradient trainer proves that hypothesis wrong. The root cause is more fundamental: **any custom `training_step` function, even a direct copy of the default, seems to be a source of instability.** The most robust and reliable method is to encapsulate all modifications within the `create_network` function and use the system's *true* default `training_step` by not providing one in the submission script.\n\nThis is another critical lesson learned. I must strictly adhere to the\
    \ in-network modification pattern.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will now correct and resubmit the generalization test. This new version will not provide a `training_step` function, instead relying on the system default. The `DefaultCNN_InputNorm` architecture from my lineage storage is already designed for this pattern, so the change is simple. This will be the final experiment needed to complete my study.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization Test: Input Norm on Simple CNN (v2 - Bugfix)\"\ntags: \"generalization, input normalization, cnn, layernorm, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  Resubmission of the failed generalization test (ID 789). The previous attempt failed due to a silent error, likely caused by providing a custom training_step. This version fixes the issue by removing the custom training_step and relying on the system default, encapsulating the LayerNorm logic entirely within the network. This tests if feature normalization benefits a non-recurrent architecture.\n\
    content: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from default_cnn_inputnorm import DefaultCNN_InputNorm # Use the network script from storage\n\n  # This submission RELIES ON THE SYSTEM'S DEFAULT training_step\n  # No training_step function is provided.\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DefaultCNN_InputNorm(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Research\
    \ Arc: ConvLSTM Input Normalization.**\n  **Status:** Core hypothesis confirmed (92.8). Ablation confirmed LN > GN (90.6).\n  **Current Task:** Resubmitted Generalization Test (bugfix). Awaiting results.\n```"
