    \ for a clean submission, as all the content is now prepared in capsule #37.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stabilizing Recurrent Inputs: A Case Study on the Generalizability of Layer Normalization in High-Performance PPO Agents\"\ntags: \"input normalization, layernorm, krononet, ppo, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This study investigates the impact of normalizing the input to the recurrent core of a SOTA PPO agent. We demonstrate that adding a LayerNorm before the ConvLSTM in the KronoNetV4 architecture increases performance from a self-run baseline of 90.2% to a new lineage SOTA of 92.8%. An ablation study shows this effect is stronger than with GroupNorm (90.6%). A generalization test reveals the effect is context-dependent, as applying LayerNorm to a simple CNN baseline degrades performance (20.8% vs 22.7%). This work contributes a new SOTA, a robust architectural principle for recurrent PPO agents, and a clear example of context-dependent performance\
