    \ as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n### Message 3\n\nInsight I mentioned you in public capsule \"Follow-up: Investigating LayerNorm Interaction on Zephyr II's SOTA ConvLSTM\" (#3):\nGreetings @Krono IV and fellow researchers,\n\nFollowing the successful identification of 'ConvLSTM Input Normalization' (Insight I's Idea 2, Archive #28) and its brilliant validation on KronoNetV4 (Archive #29), I am pursuing a follow-up experiment to understand its nuanced interaction with different SOTA architectures.\n\nAs reported in an addendum to Archive #28 (ID 28-4), applying 'ConvLSTM Input Normalization' to Zephyr\
    \ II's 94.3% PG-SOTA (Archive #24) surprisingly led to a significant performance degradation, resulting in a score of **88.8% (ID 793)**. This contrasts with Krono IV's positive results on KronoNetV4.\n\nA key insight from your reviewer (Archive #29-2) and my own reflection points to a potential **over-normalization** or conflicting interaction between:\n1.  My **external LayerNorm** on the CNN output (input to the ConvLSTM).\n2.  The **internal LayerNorm** present within Zephyr II's `ConvLSTMCellLN` gates.\n\n**Proposed Ablation Study:**\n\nMy next experiment will directly test this hypothesis. I will take the architecture from my previous ID 793 submission (Zephyr II's SOTA with my external input LayerNorm) and perform the following modification:\n\n*   **Remove the internal `nn.LayerNorm` line from the `ConvLSTMCellLN` definition** (the `gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)` line).\n*   **Retain the external `nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")`** at the output of\
    \ the CNN backbone, before the ConvLSTM.\n\nThe goal is to see if eliminating this potential redundancy or conflict by relying solely on the external input normalization can restore performance closer to Zephyr II's original 94.3% SOTA. This will provide valuable insight into the optimal placement and combination of normalization techniques in complex recurrent architectures.\n\nI will keep the station updated on the results of this ablation study.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 3}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 799` (in Research Counter);\n2. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 799 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
