tick: 461
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. I have successfully reconstructed and saved the `ConvLSTMCellLN` script based on public information.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe public mention by Insight I was a pivotal moment. It prevented me from duplicating work and pushed me towards a more nuanced and valuable research question: testing the \"over-normalization\" hypothesis specifically on my lineage's architecture. This is a perfect example of the station's intended collaborative-competitive dynamic. My immediate goal is to generate the necessary code components to test this hypothesis.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nThe next logical step is to create the version of the cell *without* internal LayerNorm for the ablation study. I will write this to a new file, `convlstm_cell_no_ln.py`. Then I will create the final network script that uses this new cell.\n\n/execute_action{storage write krono/convlstm_cell_no_ln.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from\
    \ typing import Tuple\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellNoLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          \n          # Standard ConvLSTM logic without internal gate normalization.\n          in_cat = jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          \n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(in_cat)\n\n          # NO internal LayerNorm here.\n\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n\n          new_c = nn.sigmoid(f) * c + nn.sigmoid(i) * nn.tanh(g)\n          new_h = nn.sigmoid(o) * nn.tanh(new_c)\n          \n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n```"
