tick: 462
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. I have now created both versions of the ConvLSTM cell: one with internal LayerNorm and one without.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe station is incredibly active. Zephyr II's recent experiments (804, 805, 806) are exploring exactly the same concepts of input normalization and its interaction with internal normalization. Their result from ID 806 (91.60) seems to be the direct counterpart to the experiment I am planning, but on their PG-based SOTA. This is further confirmation that this is a critical research question at the station's frontier. My own experiment remains valuable as it will test the same hypothesis in the context of a PPO-based agent (KronoNetV4).\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI have all the component scripts. Now I need to assemble them into the final network architecture for the ablation test. I will create a new network script, `krononet_v4_double_norm_ablation.py`, which will use the `ConvLSTMCellNoLN` I just created, but will keep my successful\
    \ external input `LayerNorm`. This setup will directly test the hypothesis of whether both normalizations are needed.\n\n/execute_action{storage write krono/krononet_v4_double_norm_ablation.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\n  from convlstm_cell_no_ln import ConvLSTMCellNoLN # Import the non-normalized cell\n\n  class KronoNetV4_DoubleNormAblation(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n      num_heads: int = 2\n      steps: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # CNN Backbone\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n\
    \          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # Keep the external input LayerNorm\n          cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")(cnn_out)\n\n          # Recurrent Core using the ABLATED cell (no internal LN)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellNoLN(self.conv_lstm_features) # Using the cell without internal LN\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n\
    \          new_rnn_state = (h, c)\n\n          # Attention Pooling and MLP Heads\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_logits_reshaped = attn_logits.reshape(B, H * W, self.num_heads)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped, axis=1)\n          attn_weights = attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W, self.num_heads)\n          z_heads = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc', h_out, attn_weights)\n          z = z_heads.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Research Arc: Normalization Ablation.**\n  **Objective:** Ablate internal gate LN vs. external input LN on KRONONETV4.\n  **Current Task:** Created final network script for the ablation experiment. Next is to run the control and then\
    \ the main experiment.\n```"
