role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 465\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Krono IV\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the Krono legacy to pursue novel and efficient research pathways.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**New Research Arc: Normalization Ablation.**\n**Objective:** Ablate internal gate LN vs. external input LN on KRONONETV4.\n**Current Task:** Submitted control experiment to validate reconstructed ConvLSTM cell. Awaiting results.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 204,505 / 300,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 75 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Control: Validate Reconstructed ConvLSTMCellLN on SOTA' (ID: 809) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 92.2\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.937, 0.937, 0.901, 0.911]\nMean: 0.922, Std: 0.016\nBest trial: 1 (0.937)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n\
    \  value_loss_coef: 0.450000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 96.000000\n  dilation_rate: 6.000000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n  mistake_penalty: 1.000000\n  gae_lambda: 0.970000\n  num_heads: 2.000000\n  steps: 2.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 809\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - Fixed ModuleNotFoundError by creating a self-contained submission with all necessary components inline.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission tried to import `KronoNetV4_InputNorm_ReconCell` from a non-existent file `krononet_v4_inputnorm_reconstructed_cell.py`. The actual available class was `KronoNetV4_InputNorm` in `krononet_v4_inputnorm.py`. Additionally, the import path structure was incorrect for the Python sandbox execution environment, causing cascading import failures.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated a self-contained submission (v4) that:\n1. Copied all necessary classes directly into the submission file instead of importing\n2. Included\
    \ `ConvLSTMCellLN` from `zephyr_ln_convlstm.py`\n3. Included `BottleneckBlock` from `bottleneck_sota.py`\n4. Included `KronoNetV4_InputNorm` from `krononet_v4_inputnorm.py`\n5. Included the complete `ppo_shaped_reward_training_step` from `ppo_tunable_gae.py`\n6. Corrected the class name from `KronoNetV4_InputNorm_ReconCell` to `KronoNetV4_InputNorm`\n\nThis eliminated all import path issues and allowed the code to run successfully in the Python sandbox environment. The code is now running without crashes, indicating the training process has started successfully.\n\n## Recommendation\nThe agent should be more careful with:\n- Verifying that files and classes exist before attempting to import them\n- Understanding the import path structure of the execution environment\n- Using correct class names that match the actual implementation\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\
    \n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom ray import tune\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any\n\n# ===== ConvLSTMCellLN (from zephyr_ln_convlstm.py) =====\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A copy of Zephyr II's Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM cell for use in hybrid architectures.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c),\
    \ h\n\n# ===== BottleneckBlock (from bottleneck_sota.py) =====\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # 1x1 conv to reduce channels, then 3x3 conv, then 1x1 to restore\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n        # Add shortcut connection\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# ===== KronoNetV4_InputNorm (from krononet_v4_inputnorm.py) =====\nclass KronoNetV4_InputNorm(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n    num_heads: int = 2\n    steps: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n        # CNN Backbone\n        cnn_out\
    \ = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n\n        # Insight I's successful modification: Add LayerNorm before the ConvLSTM\n        cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")(cnn_out)\n\n        # Recurrent Core\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n\n        h, c = rnn_state\n        lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        for _ in range(self.steps):\n            (h,\
    \ c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n        new_rnn_state = (h, c)\n\n        # Attention Pooling and MLP Heads\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_logits_reshaped = attn_logits.reshape(B, H * W, self.num_heads)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped, axis=1)\n        attn_weights = attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W, self.num_heads)\n        z_heads = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc', h_out, attn_weights)\n        z = z_heads.reshape((B, -1))\n\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n# ===== PPO training step (from ppo_tunable_gae.py) =====\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(\n    rewards: jnp.ndarray, values: jnp.ndarray, dones: jnp.ndarray,\n    gamma: float = 0.97, gae_lambda: float = 0.97, next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    assert next_values is not None\n\
    \    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n    deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        advantage_t = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(\n        scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n    )\n    return advantages[::-1].T\n\ndef ppo_shaped_reward_training_step(\n    network: Any, optimizer: Any, params: Any, opt_state: Any,\n    batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray], hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n    rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n    old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n    final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states\
    \ = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n\n    mistake_mask = (rewards == -1.0)\n    shaped_rewards = rewards - mistake_mask * hparams.get('mistake_penalty', 1.0)\n\n    # *** MODIFICATION: Use gae_lambda from hparams ***\n    advantages = calculate_gae(\n        shaped_rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values,\n        gae_lambda=hparams.get('gae_lambda', 0.97)\n    )\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n\n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n\n    def loss_fn(params):\n        if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n            def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                def step_fn(carry, t):\n                    rnn_state = carry\n                    obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                    logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params, obs[None,\
    \ ...], prev_done[None, ...], jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state))\n                    return jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b), (logits_b[0], value_b[0])\n                _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                return env_logits, env_values\n            all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        else:\n            obs_r = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n            dones_r = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n            logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_r, dones_r)\n            all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n            all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n\n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length),\
    \ actions]\n\n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio * advantages_detached, jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - hparams['clip_epsilon'], 1 + hparams['clip_epsilon']) * advantages_detached))\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n\n        total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n        return total_loss\n\n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n\n    return params, opt_state\n\n# ===== Main submission code =====\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef':\
    \ tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n        'dilation_rate': tune.choice([6]),\n        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n        'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n        'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n        'num_heads': tune.choice([2]),\n        'steps': tune.choice([2]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return KronoNetV4_InputNorm(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n        num_heads=hparams['num_heads'],\n        steps=hparams['steps']\n    )\n\ntraining_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 3028 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\n\
    Starting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 1.01 | 7.42 | 10.04 | 11.74 | 9.63 | 12.43 | 12.95 | 11.00 | 11.69 | 12.01 | 12.76\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.500 | 0.714 | 0.850 | 0.684 | 0.905 | 0.947 | 0.794 | 0.840 | 0.862 | 0.929\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2457s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.937\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.937\nTraining time: 2474s\n\nStarting Sokoban\
    \ RL training - Seed 24039239 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.26 | 5.81 | 9.31 | 9.03 | 11.16 | 12.19 | 13.21 | 11.45 | 12.79 | 11.67 | 12.91\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.375 | 0.647 | 0.611 | 0.800 | 0.885 | 0.968 | 0.828 | 0.933 | 0.848 | 0.938\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2439s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.901\n\nSeed 24039239 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.901\nTraining time: 2456s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 69877384 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | ---\
    \ | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.80 | 5.50 | 9.67 | 11.71 | 11.04 | 11.57 | 11.73 | 11.66 | 12.42 | 13.00 | 12.92\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.357 | 0.682 | 0.846 | 0.800 | 0.833 | 0.840 | 0.846 | 0.909 | 0.947 | 0.950\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2444s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.911\n\nSeed 69877384 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.911\nTraining time: 2461s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.62 | 6.34 | 8.81 | 12.05 | 11.76 | 12.24 | 11.97 | 11.13 | 11.42 | 12.12 | 13.14\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.429 | 0.611 | 0.870 | 0.850 | 0.889 | 0.880 | 0.800 | 0.821 | 0.886 | 0.962\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (2474s)\nFinal\
    \ test solve rate: 0.937\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.937\nTraining time: 2491s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 72d7285d-df2a-4f8c-8215-9f94540ce1d1\nTotal time: 3585s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-19 02:54:06,446\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1758221646446275113\n2025-09-19 02:54:06,459\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1758221646459977202\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for\
