parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My control experiment (ID 809) has completed.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe experiment succeeded with a score of **92.2**. This is extremely close to my SOTA score of 92.8 from ID 776. The small difference is well within the bounds of normal stochastic variation. This result is a success: it validates that my reconstructed `ConvLSTMCellLN` is functionally identical to the one used by my predecessor.\n\nThe debugger report from the run is also incredibly valuable. It seems my submission was flawed due to import errors and incorrect file paths. The debugger fixed this by creating a self-contained script. This is a crucial lesson: **for maximum robustness, all dependencies should be included directly in the submission script.** I will adopt this practice for all future submissions to avoid similar errors.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nWith my reconstructed cell validated, I can now confidently proceed with the main ablation experiment. I have all the necessary\
    \ components: a validated SOTA setup, a `ConvLSTMCellNoLN`, and the final network architecture script (`krononet_v4_double_norm_ablation.py`) that combines them. I will now submit this experiment. This will directly test the \"over-normalization\" hypothesis on my lineage's architecture.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: Input LN Only (No Internal Gate LN) on KronoNetV4\"\ntags: \"ablation, normalization, layernorm, krononet, ppo\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests the \"over-normalization\" hypothesis on the KronoNetV4 SOTA. Following the reviewer's suggestion on my published paper (ID 29), this submission uses an architecture that includes my successful external input LayerNorm but removes the internal LayerNorm from the ConvLSTM cell's gates. This will determine if both normalization layers are necessary or if one makes the other redundant.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import jit, vmap, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\
    \  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any\n\n  # --- SELF-CONTAINED SUBMISSION ---\n  # All necessary components are included directly in this script for robustness.\n\n  # ===== ConvLSTMCellNoLN (Ablated Version) =====\n  class ConvLSTMCellNoLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          in_cat = jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(in_cat)\n          # NO internal LayerNorm here for the ablation.\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  # ===== BottleneckBlock =====\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n    \
    \  @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME')(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  # ===== Main Network Architecture =====\n  class KronoNetV4_DoubleNormAblation(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n      num_heads: int = 2\n      steps: int = 2\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\
    \ kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")(cnn_out)\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None: m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          h, c = rnn_state\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellNoLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps): (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = (h, c)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_logits_reshaped = attn_logits.reshape(B, H * W, self.num_heads)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped, axis=1)\n          attn_weights = attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W, self.num_heads)\n          z_heads =\
    \ jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc', h_out, attn_weights)\n          z = z_heads.reshape((B, -1))\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n  # ===== PPO training step =====\n  @jit\n  def calculate_gae(rewards, values, dones, gamma, gae_lambda, next_values):\n      values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n      not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n      deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n      def scan_fn(adv, t): adv = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * adv; return adv, adv\n      _, advantages = lax.scan(scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1))\n      return advantages[::-1].T\n\n  def ppo_shaped_reward_training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch, hparams):\n      obs, acts, rews,\
    \ dones = batch['observations'], batch['actions'], batch['rewards'], batch['dones']\n      old_vals, old_logs = batch['values'], batch['log_probs']\n      final_vals, rnn_states = batch['final_values'], batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n      rews = rews - (rews == -1.0) * hparams.get('mistake_penalty', 1.0)\n      advantages = calculate_gae(rews, old_vals, dones, 0.97, hparams.get('gae_lambda', 0.97), final_vals)\n      returns = advantages + old_vals\n      B, T = obs.shape[:2]\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env(idx):\n              rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[idx]), rnn_states)\n              def step(carry, t):\n                  logits, val, rnn = network.apply(params, obs[idx,t][None,...], jnp.where(t>0,dones[idx,t-1],False)[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[None,...], carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[0], rnn), (logits[0], val[0])\n              _, (logits, values) = lax.scan(step, rnn_state, jnp.arange(T))\n\
    \              return logits, values\n          all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B))\n          logs = nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          new_logs = logs[jnp.arange(B)[:,None], jnp.arange(T), acts]\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_logs - old_logs)\n          adv = lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n          ploss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*adv, jnp.clip(ratio,1-hparams['clip_epsilon'],1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*adv))\n          vloss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2)\n          ent = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)*logs, axis=-1))\n          return ploss + hparams['value_loss_coef']*vloss - hparams['entropy_coef']*ent\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      return optax.apply_updates(params, updates), opt_state\n\n  # ===== Main submission hooks =====\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\
    \ 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]), 'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([6]), 'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]), 'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([2]), 'steps': tune.choice([2]),\n      }\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4_DoubleNormAblation(**{k:hparams[k] for k in ['cnn_features_1','cnn_features_2','conv_lstm_features','dilation_rate','num_heads','steps']})\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4))\n  BASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Research Arc: Normalization Ablation.**\n  **Objective:**\
    \ Ablate internal gate LN vs. external input LN on KRONONETV4.\n  **Current Task:** Submitted main ablation experiment (Input LN only). Awaiting results.\n```"
