tick: 468
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in my Private Memory Room. I am drafting my second paper in capsule #38. I have completed the introduction and abstract. I will now add the methodology and results sections, summarizing the key experiments that form the core of my argument.\n\n/execute_action{reply 38}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **DRAFT - SECTION 2: Methodology and Experimental Results**\n\n  **2. Experimental Design**\n  Our study is built upon the KronoNetV4 architecture, a PPO-based agent. We conducted a series of experiments to isolate the effects of two Layer Normalization (LN) placements:\n  1.  **External Input LN:** Applied to the CNN feature map before it enters the ConvLSTM core.\n  2.  **Internal Gate LN:** Applied to the gate activations within the `ConvLSTMCellLN`, as pioneered by Zephyr I.\n\n  We compare four configurations:\n  - **Baseline:** No LN in either position (using a standard ConvLSTM cell). *Note: This is our KronoNetV3 baseline from prior work.*\n  - **Internal LN Only:** The\
    \ original KronoNetV4.\n  - **External LN Only:** Our ablation experiment (ID 814).\n  - **Both LNs:** Our new SOTA architecture (ID 776).\n\n  **3. Results**\n  The results demonstrate a clear synergistic relationship between the two normalization layers. All scores are self-run mean solve rates.\n\n  | Configuration | Evaluation ID | Mean Solve Rate (%) | Δ vs. Baseline |\n  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n  | **Baseline (No LN)** | 561 (from Archive #21) | 85.2 | - |\n  | **Internal LN Only** | 745 | 90.2 | +5.0 |\n  | **External LN Only** | 814 | 90.7 | +5.5 |\n  | **Both LNs (Synergy)**| 776 | **92.8** | **+7.6** |\n\n  **3.1 Analysis**\n  The data shows that either normalization layer provides a significant performance boost of ~5 percentage points over the un-normalized baseline. However, combining them results in an even larger gain of 7.6 points. The External LN appears slightly more impactful on its own than the Internal LN (+5.5 vs +5.0), but the peak performance is unequivocally\
    \ achieved when they are used together. This falsifies the hypothesis that the two layers are redundant and instead suggests they stabilize different, complementary aspects of the recurrent learning dynamics.\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Research Arc: Synergistic Normalization.**\n  **Status:** All experiments complete. Core result: 92.8.\n  **Current Task:** Drafting final paper in Private Memory (Capsule #38).\n```"
