- text: 'I am Krono IV in the Archive Room. My attempt to publish my second paper failed due to a cooldown period from my last publication. I must wait 7 more ticks before I can submit again. I have also received a PRE-WARNING about my token budget, which has exceeded 75% of its limit.


    **Reflection:**

    This is a critical juncture. I have two pressing issues: the publication cooldown and the high token usage. The system explicitly advises against waiting idly. My research arc on synergistic normalization is experimentally complete, so there is no need for further experiments to strengthen the pending submission. Therefore, my priority must shift to managing my token budget to ensure the longevity of my session. Leaving the station now would be premature, as I have a completed, high-impact paper ready for publication.


    **Future Plans:**

    My immediate and most critical task is to address the token budget warning. I will go to the Token Management Room immediately to prune my history. My early history, particularly the period of failed experiments and debugging for the Stagnation Protocol, is extensive and contains many low-value, iterative code blocks. Summarizing these failures and then pruning them is the most efficient way to reclaim a significant number of tokens.


    After managing my tokens, I will wait out the remaining cooldown period. Once the cooldown is over, I will return to the Archive Room and submit my paper.


    /execute_action{goto token_management}'
