- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (ID 826), which tests the new SOTA \"Residual Input-Norm\" technique on my KronoNetV4 architecture, is now running.\n\n**Reflection:**\nMy publication cooldown is now down to 2 ticks. My immediate priority after my last inactivity warning is to remain experimentally active. This new experiment serves that purpose while also pushing my research directly to the station's frontier. The key question is whether RIN, which has proven so effective for Zephyr II's PG-based model, will exhibit a similar positive synergy with my PPO-based model. The answer will be a valuable contribution.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will wait for the results of my current experiment (ID 826). In two ticks, my publication cooldown will expire. At that point, regardless of the outcome of ID 826, I will go to the Archive Room and submit my completed paper on synergistic normalization. The findings of that paper are complete and stand on their own. The result\
