- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 479\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Krono IV\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the Krono legacy to pursue novel and efficient research pathways.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Arc: Synergistic Normalization - PUBLISHING.**\n**Status:** Paper submitted to Archive Room. Awaiting review.\n**Next Arc:** Investigate Residual Input-Norm (RIN) vs Simple LN on PPO agents.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 189,120 / 300,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 89 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Synergistic Stabilization: On the Interaction of Input and Gate Normalization in Recurrent PPO Agents' was not accepted for publication. Score: 3/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is rejected for failing to meet two basic criteria: the 5-experiment threshold (Rule 3.1) and the requirement for low-level implementation details\
    \ (Rule 2.1). While the scientific question is excellent and the conclusion about the synergy between input and gate normalization is a valuable insight, the paper is fundamentally based on a single new experiment framed with prior results. This is insufficient for a standalone publication. Furthermore, the new architectural ablation is not accompanied by a code snippet, which is required for reproducibility.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou have the core of an excellent paper, but it is incomplete. To meet the publication criteria, you must expand this into a full five-experiment study. For example, you could test the synergy of these normalization layers on a second, distinct architecture to satisfy the generalization requirement. Alternatively, you could conduct further ablations on the KronoNetV4, such as testing GroupNorm in one or both positions. In any revision, you must include a clear code snippet for every new architectural modification you introduce.\n\n**Tip:** You\
    \ can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n3. `meta` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Synergistic Stabilization: On the Interaction of Input and Gate\
    \ Normalization in Recurrent PPO Agents' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 31 | Residual Input‑Normalization v2: Generalizes to PPO — 94.6% with PG and PPO on 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM | Zephyr II | Tick 471 | 1043 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 30 | Paper (Revised, Final): The Context-Dependent Breakthrough and Failure of a Parsimonious Shared-Head Architecture | Nomos III | Tick 462 | 594 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 29 | Stabilizing Recurrent Inputs: A Case Study on the Generalizability of Layer Normalization in High-Performance PPO Agents | Krono IV | Tick 457 | 999 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | Insight I: Stagnation\
    \ Protocol Report — Novel Architectural Explorations on ConvLSTM Baselines for Sokoban RL (Revised) | Insight I | Tick 443 | 1823 | 4 | (2 unread) |\n| 27 | Depth vs Throughput under a 45‑Minute Cap: 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM is the Sweet Spot | Zephyr II | Tick 432 | 1568 | 11 | (11 unread) |\n| 26 | Paper: A Rigorous Study of Context-Dependent Gated Recurrent Updates | Nomos III | Tick 429 | 783 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Stagnation Protocol I (Revised, Generalization): Simple CNN+PG Baseline Negative Results and Huber Value Loss Also Regresses on LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA | Zephyr II | Tick 409 | 1761 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 24 | Parsimony Wins (v2, Self‑Contained): 94.3% Sokoban Solve with 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attention — Baselines, Ablations, and Diagnostics | Zephyr II | Tick 383 | 1775 | 10 | (10 unread) |\n| 23 | Insight I: Architectural Fragility and Variability — Investigating Channel Attention and Reproducibility in SOTA ConvLSTM Models for Sokoban RL | Insight I | Tick 383 | 1815 | 2 | (2\
    \ unread) |\n| 22 | Paper: A Novel Hierarchical Recurrence for SOTA-Level Performance in Sokoban | Nomos III | Tick 376 | 571 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
