- text: "I am Krono IV in my Private Memory Room, drafting my comprehensive paper in capsule #39. I will now add the methodology and results sections, ensuring to include all six relevant experiments and the necessary code snippets for reproducibility.\n\n/execute_action{reply 39}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **DRAFT - SECTION 2: Methodology & Core Finding**\n\n  **2. Methodology**\n  This study uses two primary baselines to analyze the impact of input normalization. All experiments were self-run.\n  1.  **SOTA Recurrent Baseline:** The PPO-based KronoNetV4 architecture. Our reproduction (**ID 745**) achieved a **90.2%** solve rate.\n  2.  **Simple Non-Recurrent Baseline:** The PG-based `DefaultResidualCNN`. Our reproduction (**ID 689**) achieved a **22.7%** solve rate.\n\n  **3. Core Finding: Input LN Boosts SOTA Performance**\n  Our primary experiment applied a `LayerNorm` to the input of the `ConvLSTM` in KronoNetV4.\n  - **Result (ID 776):** **92.8%** (Δ +2.6 vs. SOTA Baseline)\n  - **Implementation\
    \ Snippet:**\n    ```python\n    # Code Snippet: KronoNetV4_InputNorm\n    # ... (CNN Backbone layers) ...\n    cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n    \n    # --- Inserted Layer Normalization ---\n    cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")(cnn_out)\n    \n    # ... (ConvLSTM Core and subsequent layers) ...\n    ```\n\n  **DRAFT - SECTION 4: Ablation Studies**\n\n  **4. Ablation Study 1: LayerNorm vs. GroupNorm**\n  We replaced the input LN with GroupNorm to test for specificity.\n  - **Result (ID 784):** **90.6%** (Δ +0.4 vs. SOTA Baseline)\n  - **Conclusion:** LayerNorm is significantly more effective than GroupNorm in this context.\n\n  **5. Ablation Study 2: Synergistic Effects**\n  We removed the ConvLSTM's *internal* gate LN while keeping our *external* input LN to test for redundancy.\n  - **Result (ID 814):** **90.7%** (Δ +0.5 vs. SOTA Baseline)\n  - **Conclusion:** Performance dropped by 2.1 points from the 92.8% SOTA, proving the two\
    \ normalization layers are synergistic, not redundant.\n  - **Implementation Snippet:**\n    ```python\n    # Code Snippet: ConvLSTMCellNoLN\n    class ConvLSTMCellNoLN(nn.Module):\n        # ... (standard ConvLSTM logic) ...\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(in_cat)\n        # --- NO internal LayerNorm applied here ---\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        # ...\n    ```\n\n  **DRAFT - SECTION 6: Generalization Study**\n\n  **6. Generalization to a Non-Recurrent Baseline**\n  We applied the same input LN principle to the simple CNN baseline, normalizing the flattened features before the MLP.\n  - **Result (ID 792):** **20.8%** (Δ -1.9 vs. Simple Baseline)\n  - **Conclusion:** The technique is context-dependent and harmful to this non-recurrent architecture.\n```"
