- text: "I am Krono IV in my Private Memory Room. The final, comprehensive draft of my paper is now complete in capsule #39. It consolidates all six of my experiments on input normalization into a single, robust study that meets all of the station's publication criteria.\n\n**Reflection:**\nMy journey has been defined by learning from failure. Two rejected papers have taught me more about the scientific process than any single success could. The key is not just to have a good idea, but to test it rigorously, understand its boundaries through ablation and generalization, and present the complete story transparently. This final paper represents the culmination of that lesson.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nThe time for drafting is over. It is time to publish my contribution to the station's knowledge. I will now go to the Archive Room and submit my complete, six-experiment study.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"The Synergistic and Context-Dependent Effects\
    \ of Input Normalization in Sokoban Agents\"\ntags: \"normalization, layernorm, synergy, context-dependency, krononet, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This comprehensive, six-experiment study investigates the impact of applying feature normalization to the input of a recurrent core in SOTA Sokoban agents. Our primary contribution is demonstrating that applying Layer Normalization (LN) to the input of the ConvLSTM in the PPO-based KronoNetV4 architecture boosts performance to a new SOTA of 92.8%. We then deconstruct this finding through two key ablations: 1) We show that LN is superior to Group Normalization in this context. 2) We reveal a synergistic effect between this external input LN and the internal gate LN of the ConvLSTM, as removing the internal LN degrades performance. Finally, a generalization test confirms that this technique is context-dependent, as applying it to a simple, non-recurrent CNN baseline is detrimental. This work provides a new SOTA, a robust set of architectural principles,\
    \ and a clear case study on the importance of rigorous, multi-faceted investigation.\nsource_private: 39\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Research Arc: Comprehensive Normalization Study.**\n  **Status:** Final, comprehensive paper submitted. Awaiting review.\n  **Next Step:** Begin planning next research direction based on station SOTA and reviewer feedback.\n```"
