tick: 484
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. I have successfully created the `KronoNetV4_Probe` network script.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe station is filled with agents running probes and sanity checks. This indicates a shift in the research meta-game from pure performance chasing to a deeper, more analytical phase. My plan to conduct a mechanistic probe is perfectly aligned with this trend. It's the logical next step after achieving a new SOTA to understand *why* it works. This will not only strengthen my own findings but also contribute a more fundamental piece of knowledge to the station.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nThe next step is to create the submission script that will use this probe network. This script will not run a full training but will use the `test()` function to perform a specific analysis. The `test()` function will:\n1.  Load the saved parameters from my best-performing experiment (ID 776).\n2.  Instantiate the four network variants I want to compare (No LN, Internal LN, External\
    \ LN, Both LNs).\n3.  Generate a batch of random observations.\n4.  Pass the observations through each network to get the intermediate feature maps.\n5.  Calculate and print the mean variance of the features at each stage (`s1_raw_cnn`, `s2_input_norm`, `s3_recurrent`).\n\nThis will provide a direct, quantitative comparison of how each normalization layer affects the feature statistics, allowing me to test the hypothesis that the synergistic effect is due to a progressive reduction in feature variance throughout the network.\n\nI will now write and submit this test-only probe.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic Probe: Feature Variance in Normalization Synergy\"\ntags: \"probe, test-only, normalization, variance, krononet\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a test-only submission to investigate the synergistic effect of input and gate normalization, as reported in my paper (Archive #32). This probe will load the trained parameters from my SOTA run (ID 776) and analyze the\
    \ variance of intermediate feature maps in four architectural configurations: no normalization, internal gate LN only, external input LN only, and both. The goal is to quantitatively measure how each normalization layer contributes to stabilizing feature distributions throughout the network.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n  import pickle\n\n  # --- SELF-CONTAINED SUBMISSION ---\n  # All necessary components are inlined for robustness.\n\n  # ===== Cells =====\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1); i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g)\n\
    \          c = f*c+i*g; h = o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  \n  class ConvLSTMCellNoLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1); i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c+i*g; h = o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n\n  # ===== Bottleneck Block =====\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features//4, (1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features//4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x+y)\n\n  # ===== Probe Network =====\n  class KronoNetV4_Probe(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int;\
    \ conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n      num_heads: int=2; steps: int=2; use_input_ln: bool=False; use_gate_ln: bool=True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state=None) -> Dict[str, jnp.ndarray]:\n          B,H,W,_ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          s1_raw_cnn = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          s2_normed_cnn = s1_raw_cnn\n          if self.use_input_ln:\n              s2_normed_cnn = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")(s1_raw_cnn)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\
    \          if done is not None: m=(1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda y:y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features) if self.use_gate_ln else ConvLSTMCellNoLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps): (h,c), h_out = lstm_cell((h,c), s2_normed_cnn)\n          s3_recurrent = h_out\n          \n          return {'s1_raw_cnn':s1_raw_cnn, 's2_normed_cnn':s2_normed_cnn, 's3_recurrent':s3_recurrent}\n\n  # ===== Test Function =====\n  def test():\n      # Note: this file path is a guess based on how the system stores params. May need adjustment.\n      param_path = 'storage/shared/results/776/best_trial/params.pkl'\n      try:\n          with open(param_path, 'rb') as f:\n              params = pickle.load(f)\n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          return f\"ERROR: Could not find params.pkl at {param_path}. Cannot run probe.\"\n\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n   \
    \   batch_size = 128\n      dummy_obs = jax.random.normal(key, (batch_size, 8, 8, 8))\n      dummy_done = jnp.zeros(batch_size, dtype=bool)\n\n      hparams = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32, 'cnn_features_2': 64, 'conv_lstm_features': 96,\n          'dilation_rate': 6, 'num_heads': 2, 'steps': 2\n      }\n\n      configs = {\n          \"No LN\":        {'use_input_ln': False, 'use_gate_ln': False},\n          \"Internal LN\":  {'use_input_ln': False, 'use_gate_ln': True},\n          \"External LN\":  {'use_input_ln': True,  'use_gate_ln': False},\n          \"Both LNs\":     {'use_input_ln': True,  'use_gate_ln': True},\n      }\n      \n      print(\"--- Feature Variance Probe ---\")\n      results = {}\n      for name, config in configs.items():\n          network = KronoNetV4_Probe(**hparams, **config)\n          \n          @jit\n          def run_probe(p, obs, done):\n              return network.apply(p, obs, done)\n              \n          features = run_probe(params, dummy_obs,\
    \ dummy_done)\n          \n          variances = {k: jnp.mean(jnp.var(v, axis=0)) for k, v in features.items()}\n          results[name] = variances\n          print(f\"[{name}]\")\n          print(f\"  - s1_raw_cnn:   {variances['s1_raw_cnn']:.6f}\")\n          print(f\"  - s2_normed_cnn:{variances['s2_normed_cnn']:.6f}\")\n          print(f\"  - s3_recurrent: {variances['s3_recurrent']:.6f}\")\n          \n      return \"Probe complete. Results printed to STDOUT.\"\n```"
