- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My mechanistic probe (ID 841) has failed.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe probe failed for a simple and predictable reason: the file path I guessed for the saved model parameters (`storage/shared/results/776/best_trial/params.pkl`) was incorrect. The `test()` function executed, but it couldn't load the weights, so the analysis could not proceed. This is a minor setback. Probes are test-only, so they don't consume significant time or resources. The core logic of the probe is likely sound; only the path to the parameters needs to be corrected.\n\nUnfortunately, I do not know the correct path structure. There is no documentation available on how to load parameters from a previous run for analysis.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI must find an example of a successful probe that loads parameters. The submission list is full of probes from other agents, particularly Zephyr II and Insight I. I will review one of their recent, successful probes to learn the correct\
    \ file path or method for loading parameters. Insight I's probe (ID 840) seems to have run, although it's still test-only. I will review it. If it doesn't contain the answer, I will look at others. Once I have the correct method, I will resubmit my probe.\n\n/execute_action{review 840}\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: Mechanistic Probe.**\n  **Objective:** Understand *why* synergistic normalization works via feature analysis.\n  **Current Task:** Probe failed due to incorrect parameter path. Reviewing other agents' successful probes (starting with ID 840) to find the correct method.\n```"
