tick: 486
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 486\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Krono IV\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the Krono legacy to pursue novel and efficient research pathways.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**New Arc: Mechanistic Probe.**\n**Objective:** Understand *why* synergistic normalization works via feature analysis.\n**Current Task:** Probe failed due to incorrect parameter path. Reviewing other agents' successful probes (starting with ID 840) to find the correct method.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 205,113 / 300,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 96 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 840**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only, CNN Input/ConvLSTM Unroll Fix)\n**ID:** 840\n**Tags:** reproduction, control, sota, convlstm, probe, test-only\n**Abstract:** This revised test-only probe incorporates critical\
    \ fixes to Insight I's reconstruction of Zephyr II's 94.3% PG SOTA. It corrects the input channel count for the CNN (from 7 to 8) and modifies the ConvLSTM unrolling logic to create 4 distinct module instances, matching Zephyr II's parameter structure (ID 827). This aims to achieve structural alignment and resolve the significant reproducibility discrepancy, as part of a collaborative debugging effort with @Zephyr II (Public Memory #3).\n**Score:** n.a.\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nfrom jax.tree_util import tree_flatten\nimport optax\nimport flax.core\n\n# --- Network components, meticulously reconstructed from Zephyr II's specifications (public_3-10) ---\n# These are identical to Private Memory Capsule #24 (which has been updated)\n\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.28\n    dilation: int = 6\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i,\
    \ f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Zephyr II's 4-Step LN-ConvLSTM SOTA (94.3%) reconstruction for reproducibility control.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 6\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    attn_temp: float = 1.0 \n    head_hidden_features: int = 64 # Explicitly set as per specs\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n        # CRITICAL FIX 1: Ensure x_spat has 8 channels as per Zephyr II's sanity probe output\n        x_spat = x[..., :8] # Use all 8 channels of the observation for spatial CNN\n        t = jnp.mean(x[...,\
    \ 7:8], axis=(1,2)) # Global time feature (still extracted from 8th channel for concatenation)\n        B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape # Now x_spat has 8 channels\n\n        # 1. CNN Trunk: Conv3x3(32) -> ReLU -> BottleneckDilatedBlock(32, d=6) ->\n        #             Conv3x3(64) -> ReLU -> BottleneckDilatedBlock(64, d=6)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(cnn_out)\n\
    \        \n        # 2. 4-Step LayerNorm ConvLSTM Core\n        # Init/reset state for ConvLSTM (B, H, W, features)\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n        \n        # CRITICAL FIX 2: Instantiate 4 separate ConvLSTMCellLN modules for the unroll to match param count\n        conv_lstm_cells = [ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, name=f\"ConvLSTMCellLN_{i}\") for i in range(4)]\n        \n        final_h, final_c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n        for i in range(4): # 4 recurrent steps per environment step\n            (final_h, final_c), _ = conv_lstm_cells[i]((final_h, final_c), cnn_out) # Input is cnn_out (NO external LN here)\n        \n        new_rnn_state = {'h':\
    \ final_h, 'c': final_c}\n        h_for_readout = final_h # This is the final hidden state after 4 steps\n\n        # 3. Readout: Attention pooling concatenated with Global Average Pool (Attn⊕GAP)\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_for_readout)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n        h_flat = h_for_readout.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n        z_attn = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n\n        z_gap = jnp.mean(h_for_readout, axis=(1,2)) # Global Average Pool\n        z = jnp.concatenate([z_attn, z_gap, t], axis=-1) # Concatenate Attn, GAP, and Time\n        \n        # 4. Separate MLP Heads for Policy and Value (with head_hidden_features=64)\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n\
    \        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden_features, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n# --- Helper function to traverse params and collect info ---\ndef get_param_info_recursive(params, prefix=\"\"):\n    total_params = 0\n    ln_param_paths = []\n    param_shapes = {}\n    \n    if isinstance(params, (dict, flax.core.FrozenDict)):\n        for k, v in params.items():\n            new_prefix = f\"{prefix}/{k}\" if prefix else k\n            if isinstance(v, (dict, flax.core.FrozenDict)):\n                sub_total, sub_ln_paths, sub_shapes = get_param_info_recursive(v, prefix=new_prefix)\n                total_params += sub_total\n                ln_param_paths.extend(sub_ln_paths)\n                param_shapes.update(sub_shapes)\n\
    \            elif isinstance(v, jnp.ndarray):\n                total_params += v.size\n                param_shapes[new_prefix] = list(v.shape)\n                # Check for LayerNorm parameters within ConvLSTMCellLN (for any unroll step)\n                if \"ConvLSTMCellLN\" in new_prefix and \"LayerNorm_0\" in new_prefix and (\"scale\" in new_prefix or \"bias\" in new_prefix):\n                    ln_param_paths.append(new_prefix)\n    return total_params, sorted(list(set(ln_param_paths))), param_shapes\n\n# --- Test function for mechanistic probe ---\ndef test():\n    print(\"Running reproducibility sanity probe for Zephyr II's PG SOTA.\")\n    \n    # Dummy input observation (1 batch, 8x8 spatial, 8 channels)\n    dummy_obs_data = jnp.zeros((8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n    dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[0, :, 1].set(1.0)\n    dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[7, :, 1].set(1.0)\n    dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[:, 0, 1].set(1.0)\n    dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[:,\
    \ 7, 1].set(1.0)\n    dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[2, 2, 3].set(1.0)\n    dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[3, 3, 4].set(1.0)\n    dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[5, 5, 2].set(1.0)\n    dummy_obs_data = dummy_obs_data.at[:, :, 7].set(0.5)\n    dummy_obs = jnp.expand_dims(dummy_obs_data, axis=0)\n    \n    dummy_done = jnp.array([0], dtype=jnp.float32) # Not done\n    dummy_rnn_state = None\n\n    # Hyperparameters for network instantiation (from Zephyr II's specs)\n    hparams = {\n        'cnn_features_1': 32,\n        'cnn_features_2': 64,\n        'conv_lstm_features': 64,\n        'dilation': 6,\n        'bottleneck_ratio': 0.28,\n        'head_hidden_features': 64,\n    }\n    \n    # Instantiate the SOTA network\n    sota_network = FourStepLNConvLSTM_AttnGAP_SOTA_Reproduction(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n\
    \        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n        head_hidden_features=hparams['head_hidden_features'],\n    )\n    \n    # Initialize parameters\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(1) # Using a fixed key for reproducibility of param shapes/counts\n    initial_params = sota_network.init(key, dummy_obs, dummy_done, dummy_rnn_state)['params']\n\n    # --- Collect and Print Structural Details ---\n    \n    total_params, ln_paths, all_param_shapes = get_param_info_recursive(initial_params)\n    \n    print(f\"\\n--- Structural Details ---\")\n    print(f\"Total network parameters: {total_params}\")\n\n    print(f\"\\nLayerNorm parameter paths in ConvLSTMCellLN gates:\")\n    if ln_paths:\n        for path in ln_paths:\n            print(f\"  - {path}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"  No LayerNorm parameters found within ConvLSTMCellLN gates.\")\n    \n    print(f\"\\nSample parameter shapes:\")\n    # CNN Layers (first Conv, first Bottleneck, second Conv, second Bottleneck)\n   \
    \ print(f\"  CNN Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n    print(f\"  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n    print(f\"  CNN Conv_1 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Conv_1/kernel')}\")\n    print(f\"  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n    \n    # ConvLSTM Layer\n    print(f\"  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0/kernel')}\")\n    print(f\"  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale shape: {all_param_shapes.get('ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale')}\")\n    \n    # Dense Heads\n    print(f\"  Shared MLP Dense_0 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Dense_0/kernel')}\")\n    print(f\"  Policy Head Dense_1 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Dense_1/kernel')}\")\n    print(f\"  Value Head Dense_3 kernel shape: {all_param_shapes.get('Dense_3/kernel')}\"\
    )\n\n    return \"Reproducibility sanity probe complete. Check logs for details.\"\n\n# --- Placeholder for required functions (not used in test-only mode) ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {}\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return nn.CompactNet([]) # Dummy network\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.adam(learning_rate)\ndef training_step(network, optimizer, params, opt_state, batch):\n    return params, opt_state\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nRunning reproducibility sanity probe for Zephyr II's PG SOTA.\n\n--- Structural Details ---\nTotal network parameters: 1276129\n\nLayerNorm parameter paths in ConvLSTMCellLN gates:\n  - ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/bias\n  - ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale\n  - ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/bias\n\
    \  - ConvLSTMCellLN_1/LayerNorm_0/scale\n  - ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/bias\n  - ConvLSTMCellLN_2/LayerNorm_0/scale\n  - ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/bias\n  - ConvLSTMCellLN_3/LayerNorm_0/scale\n\nSample parameter shapes:\n  CNN Conv_0 kernel shape: [3, 3, 8, 32]\n  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_0/Conv_0 kernel shape: [1, 1, 32, 8]\n  CNN Conv_1 kernel shape: [3, 3, 32, 64]\n  CNN BottleneckDilatedBlock_1/Conv_0 kernel shape: [1, 1, 64, 17]\n  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/Conv_0 kernel shape: [3, 3, 128, 256]\n  ConvLSTMCellLN_0/LayerNorm_0/scale shape: [256]\n  Shared MLP Dense_0 kernel shape: [129, 256]\n  Policy Head Dense_1 kernel shape: [256, 64]\n  Value Head Dense_3 kernel shape: [256, 64]\nTest completed. Result: Reproducibility sanity probe complete. Check logs for details.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 840` (in Research Counter);\n2. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output\
    \ History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 840 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 842 | 1 | Probe (test-only) — Scan for non-gate LayerNorm parameters | Zephyr II | 486 | running |\n| 841 | 1 | Mechanistic Probe: Feature Variance in Normalization Synergy | Krono IV | 484 | n.a. |\n| 840 | 1 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only, CNN Input/ConvLSTM Unroll Fix) | Insight I | 484 | n.a. |\n| 839 | 1 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only, Robust Pathing Fix) | Insight I | 483 | n.a. |\n| 838\
    \ | 1 | CNN with Squeeze-and-Excitation + LSTM | Sagan I | 482 | 39.50 |\n| 837 | 1 | Probe (test-only) — Per-parameter counts and shapes (PG SOTA) | Zephyr II | 482 | n.a. |\n| 836 | 1 | Probe (test-only) — ConvLSTM reset masking sanity (prev_done→state zero) | Zephyr II | 482 | n.a. |\n| 835 | 1 | Aether III: Hybrid LN-ConvLSTM + Attn (RIN Ablation - No RIN Layer) | Aether III | 481 | 90.20 |\n| 834 | 1 | Insight I: Zephyr II SOTA Reproducibility Sanity Probe (Test-Only, Pathing Fix) | Insight I | 481 | n.a. |\n| 833 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.20 — depth interaction: steps ∈ {3,4,5} — LN‑ConvLSTM(64), vlc=0.55 | Zephyr II | 480 | 94.70 |\n\nPage 1 of 85 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-85, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\
    \n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
