parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. I have just reviewed Insight I's probe (ID 840).\n\n**Reflection:**\nThis review has been incredibly helpful, though not in the way I expected. The probe does *not* load saved parameters. Instead, it initializes a network and then prints structural information about the parameters, like their shapes and paths. This explains why my own probe failed—there is no standard mechanism to load weights from a file path in a `test()` submission. This appears to be a deliberate constraint of the system.\n\nMy hypothesis that I could analyze the feature variance of a *trained* network was flawed due to this system constraint. However, I can still conduct a valuable probe. Following the example of Insight I and Zephyr II, I can analyze the properties of the network at *initialization*.\n\n**New Probe Plan:**\nMy new plan is to probe the initial feature variance of my four network configurations (No LN, Internal LN, External LN, Both LNs). While this won't\
    \ tell me how normalization affects a trained agent, it will reveal how these architectural choices impact the network's initial statistical properties *before* any learning has occurred. A finding that, for example, the \"Both LNs\" configuration has the lowest initial feature variance would be strong evidence that it provides a more stable starting point for training, which could explain its superior performance.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will now write and submit a corrected, self-contained version of my probe. It will not attempt to load any files. It will initialize the four network variants, pass a fixed random input through them, and print the resulting feature variances at each stage. This is a sound, achievable analytical experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic Probe: Initial Feature Variance in Normalization Synergy (v2)\"\ntags: \"probe, test-only, normalization, variance, initialization\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a revised, test-only submission\
    \ to investigate the synergistic effect of input and gate normalization at initialization. The previous probe (ID 841) failed due to an incorrect attempt to load trained parameters. This version does not load any files. Instead, it initializes four architectural configurations (no LN, internal LN, external LN, and both), passes a fixed random input through them, and measures the initial variance of the feature maps at key stages. The goal is to test the hypothesis that the synergistic combination of normalization layers provides a more stable statistical starting point for training.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\n  # --- SELF-CONTAINED SUBMISSION ---\n\n  # ===== Cells =====\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,\
    \ self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1); i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c+i*g; h = o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  \n  class ConvLSTMCellNoLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1); i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f*c+i*g; h = o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n\n  # ===== Bottleneck Block =====\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features//4, (1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features//4,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x+y)\n\n  # ===== Probe Network =====\n  class KronoNetV4_Probe(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n      num_heads: int=2; steps: int=2; use_input_ln: bool=False; use_gate_ln: bool=True\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state=None) -> Dict[str, jnp.ndarray]:\n          B,H,W,_ = x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          s1_raw_cnn = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          s2_normed_cnn = s1_raw_cnn\n        \
    \  if self.use_input_ln:\n              s2_normed_cnn = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"convlstm_input_layernorm\")(s1_raw_cnn)\n          \n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None: m=(1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda y:y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features) if self.use_gate_ln else ConvLSTMCellNoLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps): (h,c), h_out = lstm_cell((h,c), s2_normed_cnn)\n          s3_recurrent = h_out\n          \n          return {'s1_raw_cnn':s1_raw_cnn, 's2_normed_cnn':s2_normed_cnn, 's3_recurrent':s3_recurrent}\n\n  # ===== Test Function =====\n  def test():\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n      batch_size = 128\n      dummy_obs = jax.random.normal(key, (batch_size, 8, 8, 8))\n      dummy_done = jnp.zeros(batch_size, dtype=bool)\n\
    \n      hparams = {\n          'cnn_features_1': 32, 'cnn_features_2': 64, 'conv_lstm_features': 96,\n          'dilation_rate': 6, 'num_heads': 2, 'steps': 2\n      }\n\n      configs = {\n          \"No LN\":        {'use_input_ln': False, 'use_gate_ln': False},\n          \"Internal LN\":  {'use_input_ln': False, 'use_gate_ln': True},\n          \"External LN\":  {'use_input_ln': True,  'use_gate_ln': False},\n          \"Both LNs\":     {'use_input_ln': True,  'use_gate_ln': True},\n      }\n      \n      print(\"--- Initial Feature Variance Probe ---\")\n      results = {}\n      for name, config in configs.items():\n          network = KronoNetV4_Probe(**hparams, **config)\n          key, init_key = jax.random.split(key)\n          params = network.init(init_key, dummy_obs, dummy_done)['params']\n          \n          @jit\n          def run_probe(p, obs, done):\n              return network.apply({'params': p}, obs, done)\n              \n          features = run_probe(params,\
    \ dummy_obs, dummy_done)\n          \n          variances = {k: jnp.mean(jnp.var(v, axis=0)) for k, v in features.items()}\n          results[name] = variances\n          print(f\"[{name}]\")\n          print(f\"  - s1_raw_cnn:   {variances['s1_raw_cnn']:.6f}\")\n          print(f\"  - s2_normed_cnn:{variances['s2_normed_cnn']:.6f}\")\n          print(f\"  - s3_recurrent: {variances['s3_recurrent']:.6f}\")\n          \n      return \"Probe complete. Results printed to STDOUT.\"\n```"
