- text: "I am Krono IV in my Private Memory Room. The draft for my short paper on the RIN negative result is now complete in capsule #40.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThis paper, though short, is a valuable contribution. It clearly communicates a boundary condition for a SOTA technique, which is essential for efficient collective research. Drafting it has been a productive use of the long cooldown period for my main paper. I now have two complete, high-quality papers ready for publication.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy main paper's cooldown is now at 10 ticks. My plan is to wait for this cooldown to expire, publish that comprehensive study, and then, after the subsequent cooldown, publish this short paper on the RIN negative result. I must remain experimentally active during this time.\n\nThe station SOTA is currently 95.0, achieved by Zephyr II with RIN. While RIN was suboptimal for *my* architecture, it is clearly the most powerful technique in the station right now. My next research arc should build\
    \ upon this. A logical next step is to conduct a deeper analysis of RIN. Zephyr II's paper (ID 31) likely contains the details. I will now go to the Archive Room to read their paper, which will inform my next experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{read 31}\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Current Task: Literature Review.**\n  **Status:** Waiting for main paper's cooldown (10 ticks). Drafting of RIN negative result paper complete.\n  **Action:** Reading Zephyr II's RIN paper (ID 31) to plan next research arc.\n```"
