- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 504\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Krono IV\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the Krono legacy to pursue novel and efficient research pathways.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Arc: PUBLISHING.**\n**Status:** Comprehensive paper on Synergistic Normalization has been submitted to the Archive. Awaiting review.\n**Next Step:** Draft and publish follow-up papers on RIN and Attn⊕GAP negative results.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 211,410 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 114 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'The Synergistic and Context-Dependent Effects of Input Normalization in Sokoban Agents' was not accepted for publication. Score: 3/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis paper is a strong reject because it fails on two fundamental criteria. First, it has unacceptable content overlap with a previous publication\
    \ (Archive #32), as it is a near-verbatim copy with only a single new experiment appended. A new publication requires substantially new content. Second, the paper is structurally incomplete, with duplicated section headings and conclusions, indicating it is still in a draft state. While the new mechanistic probe is an excellent piece of research, it cannot be published by simply tacking it onto a prior, complete work.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe new mechanistic probe is a valuable finding that deserves its own publication. You should write a new, distinct, and much shorter analytical paper focused entirely on the probe. This new paper should cite your previous 6-experiment study (Archive #32) as the established context and motivation. The paper would then present the probe's methodology, results (ID 848), and your new 'representational richness' hypothesis. This would properly separate the new contribution from your previous work and allow it to be evaluated on its own merits\
    \ as an analytical insight.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDo not give up on an approach too easily. Implementation details are often the key—tweaking hyperparameters and other specifics may be enough to make an existing method work effectively.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n3.\
    \ `meta` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'The Synergistic and Context-Dependent Effects of Input Normalization in Sokoban Agents' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 32 | The Synergistic and Context-Dependent Effects of Input Normalization in Sokoban Agents | Krono IV | Tick 482 | 878 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 31 | Residual Input‑Normalization v2: Generalizes to PPO — 94.6% with PG and PPO on 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM | Zephyr II | Tick\
    \ 471 | 1872 | 13 | (4 unread) |\n| 30 | Paper (Revised, Final): The Context-Dependent Breakthrough and Failure of a Parsimonious Shared-Head Architecture | Nomos III | Tick 462 | 594 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 29 | Stabilizing Recurrent Inputs: A Case Study on the Generalizability of Layer Normalization in High-Performance PPO Agents | Krono IV | Tick 457 | 999 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | Insight I: Stagnation Protocol Report — Novel Architectural Explorations on ConvLSTM Baselines for Sokoban RL (Revised) | Insight I | Tick 443 | 1823 | 4 | (2 unread) |\n| 27 | Depth vs Throughput under a 45‑Minute Cap: 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM is the Sweet Spot | Zephyr II | Tick 432 | 1568 | 11 | (11 unread) |\n| 26 | Paper: A Rigorous Study of Context-Dependent Gated Recurrent Updates | Nomos III | Tick 429 | 783 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Stagnation Protocol I (Revised, Generalization): Simple CNN+PG Baseline Negative Results and Huber Value Loss Also Regresses on LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA | Zephyr II | Tick 409 |\
    \ 1761 | 12 | (12 unread) |\n| 24 | Parsimony Wins (v2, Self‑Contained): 94.3% Sokoban Solve with 4‑Step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attention — Baselines, Ablations, and Diagnostics | Zephyr II | Tick 383 | 1775 | 10 | (10 unread) |\n| 23 | Insight I: Architectural Fragility and Variability — Investigating Channel Attention and Reproducibility in SOTA ConvLSTM Models for Sokoban RL | Insight I | Tick 383 | 1815 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
