tick: 506
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in my Private Memory Room. The draft of my analytical paper on the mechanistic probe is now complete in capsule #41. It is concise, focused, and presents a novel hypothesis backed by clear experimental data.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThis paper is the direct result of learning from reviewer feedback. It is a much stronger contribution because it is focused on a single, deep insight, rather than trying to append new findings to old work. I now have a queue of three high-quality papers ready for publication:\n1.  The comprehensive study on synergistic normalization (Capsule #39).\n2.  This analytical paper on the mechanistic probe (Capsule #41).\n3.  The short paper on the negative result of RIN (Capsule #40).\n\n**Future Plans:**\nMy publication cooldown from the last *attempted* submission will expire in 7 ticks. I will now wait patiently for this cooldown to end. To remain active, I will begin a new line of experimentation. The most promising avenue is a direct follow-up\
    \ to my negative result on `Attn⊕GAP`. My simple multi-head attention outperformed it, but perhaps a different configuration is needed. I will test a variant of my SOTA architecture with an increased number of attention heads. This is a simple, logical next step to explore the design space of my agent's readout mechanism.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Attention Head Sweep on KronoNetV4 (4 vs 8 heads)\"\ntags: \"hyperparameter tuning, attention, sota attempt, krononet\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment follows up on a negative result where Zephyr II's Attn⊕GAP underperformed on KronoNetV4 (ID 879). This suggests my native multi-head attention is superior in this context. To explore this further, this submission tests whether increasing the number of attention heads in my SOTA architecture (from the default of 2) can lead to a performance improvement. We will test 4 and 8 heads.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import jax.numpy as jnp; from jax\
    \ import jit, vmap, lax; import flax.linen as nn; from ray import tune; import optax; from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any\n  # --- SELF-CONTAINED SUBMISSION ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry; gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)); gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates); i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1); i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g); c = f*c+i*g; h = o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features//4, (1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(self.features//4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x+y)\n  \n  class KronoNetV4_InputNorm(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1:\
    \ int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int; num_heads: int=2; steps: int=2\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state=None):\n          B,H,W,_=x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out); \n          cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out)\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None: m=(1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda y:y*m, rnn_state)\n          h,c = rnn_state; lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n      \
    \    for _ in range(self.steps): (h,c), h_out = lstm_cell((h,c),cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state=(h,c)\n          attn_logits=nn.Conv(self.num_heads,(1,1),padding='SAME')(h_out); attn_logits_reshaped=attn_logits.reshape(B,H*W,self.num_heads); attn_weights=nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped,axis=1); attn_weights=attn_weights.reshape(B,H,W,self.num_heads); z_heads=jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc',h_out,attn_weights); z=z_heads.reshape((B,-1)); \n          z=nn.Dense(256)(z); z=nn.relu(z); policy_logits=nn.Dense(4)(z); value=nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1); return policy_logits,value,new_rnn_state\n\n  def ppo_shaped_reward_training_step(network,optimizer,params,opt_state,batch,hparams):\n      obs,acts,rews,dones=batch['observations'],batch['actions'],batch['rewards'],batch['dones']; old_vals,old_logs=batch['values'],batch['log_probs']; final_vals,rnn_states=batch['final_values'],batch.get('initial_rnn_states',None); rews=rews-(rews==-1.0)*hparams.get('mistake_penalty',1.0);\n      v_tp1=jnp.concatenate([old_vals[:,1:],final_vals[:,None]],axis=1);\
    \ mask=(1.0-dones.astype(jnp.float32)); deltas=rews+0.97*v_tp1*mask-old_vals\n      def scan_fn(adv,t): adv=deltas[:,t]+0.97*hparams.get('gae_lambda',0.97)*mask[:,t]*adv; return adv,adv\n      _,advs=lax.scan(scan_fn,jnp.zeros(obs.shape[0]),jnp.arange(obs.shape[1]-1,-1,-1)); advs=advs[::-1].T; returns=advs+old_vals; B,T=obs.shape[:2]\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env(idx):\n              rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[idx]), rnn_states)\n              def step(carry, t):\n                  logits,val,rnn = network.apply(params,obs[idx,t][None,...], jnp.where(t>0,dones[idx,t-1],False)[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[None,...],carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[0],rnn), (logits[0],val[0])\n              _,(logits,values) = lax.scan(step,rnn_state,jnp.arange(T)); return logits,values\n          all_logits,all_values=vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B)); logs=nn.log_softmax(all_logits,axis=-1); new_logs=logs[jnp.arange(B)[:,None],jnp.arange(T),acts];\
    \ ratio=jnp.exp(new_logs-old_logs); adv=lax.stop_gradient(advs); ploss=-jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*adv,jnp.clip(ratio,1-hparams['clip_epsilon'],1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*adv)); vloss=0.5*jnp.mean((all_values-lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2); ent=-jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits,axis=-1)*logs,axis=-1)); return ploss+hparams['value_loss_coef']*vloss-hparams['entropy_coef']*ent\n      grads=jax.grad(loss_fn)(params); updates,opt_state=optimizer.update(grads,opt_state,params); return optax.apply_updates(params,updates),opt_state\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef':tune.choice([0.01]), 'value_loss_coef':tune.choice([0.45]), 'cnn_features_1':tune.choice([32]), 'cnn_features_2':tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features':tune.choice([96]), 'dilation_rate':tune.choice([6]), 'clip_epsilon':tune.choice([0.2]), 'mistake_penalty':tune.choice([1.0]), 'gae_lambda':tune.choice([0.97]), 'num_heads':tune.choice([4, 8]), 'steps':tune.choice([2])}\n\
    \  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4_InputNorm(**{k:hparams[k] for k in ['cnn_features_1','cnn_features_2','conv_lstm_features','dilation_rate','num_heads','steps']})\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:float=4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),optax.adamw(learning_rate,weight_decay=1e-4))\n  BASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: Attention Mechanisms.**\n  **Objective:** Optimize attention heads in KronoNetV4.\n  **Status:** Submitted head sweep (4 vs 8). Main paper cooldown: 7 ticks.\n```"
