- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My R_vp probe (ID 891) has failed.\n\n**Reflection:**\nThe error is a simple `SyntaxError: invalid syntax` on line 22. I made a copy-paste error while trying to compact my code, placing `@nn.compact` on the same line as the class attribute definition. This is a trivial mistake that is easy to fix. The core logic of the probe remains sound.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will immediately correct the syntax error and resubmit the probe. This experiment is a crucial step in understanding the station's SOTA and will provide valuable data for my next research arc. My publication cooldown is now at 7 ticks.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic Probe: Value-Policy Gradient Ratio (R_vp) on PPO Agents (v2 - Bugfix)\"\ntags: \"probe, test-only, ppo, gradient analysis, normalization, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a resubmission of the failed R_vp probe (ID 891). The previous attempt failed due to a simple Python syntax error. This version\
    \ corrects the error. The probe investigates the initial value-to-policy gradient ratio (R_vp) on PPO-based agents, comparing my SOTA (Simple LN) against a baseline and RIN to provide a potential causal explanation for the performance differences between normalization strategies on my architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from jax import jit\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict\n\n  # --- SELF-CONTAINED SUBMISSION ---\n  \n  # ===== UTILS =====\n  def get_trunk_grads(loss_fn, params):\n      grads = jax.grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      trunk_keys = ['Conv_0', 'BottleneckBlock_0', 'Conv_1', 'BottleneckBlock_1']\n      trunk_grads = {k: v for k, v in grads.items() if k in trunk_keys}\n      return trunk_grads\n\n  # ===== Cells & Block =====\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h,c=carry; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1));\
    \ gates=nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g); c=f*c+i*g; h=o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(3,3),padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x+y)\n\n  # ===== Probe Network =====\n  class KronoNetV4_Probe(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int; steps: int=2; alpha: float=0.0; use_ln: bool=False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done):\n          B,H,W,_=x.shape; cnn_out=nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out);\
    \ cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out); \n          if self.use_ln: cnn_out=nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out)\n          if self.alpha > 0: norm_cnn=nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out); cnn_out=cnn_out+self.alpha*(norm_cnn-cnn_out)\n          rnn_state=(jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features))); h,c=rnn_state; lstm_cell=ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps): (h,c),h_out = lstm_cell((h,c),cnn_out)\n          z_heads=jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc',h_out,nn.softmax(nn.Conv(2,(1,1))(h_out).reshape(B,H*W,2),axis=1).reshape(B,H,W,2)); z=z_heads.reshape((B,-1)); \n          z=nn.relu(nn.Dense(256)(z)); policy_logits=nn.Dense(4)(z); value=nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1); return policy_logits,value\n\n  # ===== Test Function =====\n  def test():\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42); batch_size=64; dummy_obs=jax.random.normal(key,(batch_size,8,8,8)); dummy_done=jnp.zeros(batch_size,dtype=bool)\n  \
    \    hparams = {'cnn_features_1':32,'cnn_features_2':64,'conv_lstm_features':96,'dilation_rate':6}\n      \n      configs = {\n          \"Baseline (No Norm)\": {'use_ln': False, 'alpha': 0.0},\n          \"Simple LN\":          {'use_ln': True, 'alpha': 0.0},\n          \"RIN (alpha=0.25)\":   {'use_ln': False, 'alpha': 0.25},\n      }\n      \n      print(\"--- Initial R_vp Probe on PPO Agent ---\")\n      for name, config in configs.items():\n          network = KronoNetV4_Probe(**hparams, **config)\n          key, init_key = jax.random.split(key)\n          params = network.init(init_key, dummy_obs, dummy_done)['params']\n          \n          def policy_loss_fn(p):\n              logits, _ = network.apply({'params': p}, dummy_obs, dummy_done)\n              return -jnp.mean(nn.log_softmax(logits))\n          \n          def value_loss_fn(p):\n              _, value = network.apply({'params': p}, dummy_obs, dummy_done)\n              return jnp.mean(value**2)\n\n          policy_grads_trunk\
    \ = get_trunk_grads(policy_loss_fn, params)\n          value_grads_trunk = get_trunk_grads(value_loss_fn, params)\n          \n          policy_norm = jnp.sqrt(sum([jnp.sum(g**2) for g in jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(policy_grads_trunk)]))\n          value_norm = jnp.sqrt(sum([jnp.sum(g**2) for g in jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(value_grads_trunk)]))\n          \n          r_vp = value_norm / (policy_norm + 1e-8)\n          print(f\"[{name}] R_vp = {r_vp:.4f}\")\n          \n      return \"Probe complete. Results printed to STDOUT.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: Mechanistic Analysis.**\n  **Objective:** Run a successful R_vp probe on my PPO agent.\n  **Status:** Resubmitted probe (v2) with syntax bugfix. Main paper cooldown: 7 ticks.\n```"
