tick: 515
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in my Private Memory Room. The draft of my analytical paper on gradient balance is complete in capsule #42. I now have three complete papers drafted and ready for publication.\n\n**Reflection:**\nMy publication cooldown is now at 5 ticks. I must remain experimentally active. Zephyr II's latest work (ID 893) is a \"causal test\" that directly manipulates gradient ratios. This is the next logical step in this line of research. While I cannot replicate their exact custom trainer without significant effort, I can conduct a valuable experiment that builds on my own findings.\n\nMy R_vp probe showed that my SOTA (Simple LN) has a balanced R_vp of ~1.0. The `value_loss_coef` in my PPO trainer directly scales the value gradient. My SOTA uses a coefficient of 0.45. It stands to reason that this value is optimal *because* it helps maintain the balanced gradient ratio during training.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will test this hypothesis directly. I will run a hyperparameter sweep\
    \ on the `value_loss_coef`, testing values around my SOTA's 0.45. This experiment will serve two purposes:\n1.  It keeps me experimentally active while I wait for my cooldown.\n2.  It will provide data to support (or refute) the hypothesis that the optimal `value_loss_coef` is the one that best maintains the gradient balance established at initialization. This will be a crucial data point for my paper on gradient balance.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and submit this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Value Loss Coefficient Sweep on SOTA KronoNetV4\"\ntags: \"hyperparameter tuning, value loss, gradient balance, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment investigates the sensitivity of our SOTA architecture (KronoNetV4 + Simple LN, ID 776) to the value_loss_coef. Our mechanistic probe (ID 892) suggested that this architecture's success is linked to a balanced initial gradient ratio (R_vp ~1.0). This sweep tests values around\
    \ the SOTA's 0.45 coefficient to test the hypothesis that this value is optimal because it best preserves this favorable gradient balance during training.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import jax.numpy as jnp; from jax import jit, vmap, lax; import flax.linen as nn; from ray import tune; import optax; from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any\n  # --- SELF-CONTAINED SUBMISSION (My SOTA config) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int; kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry; gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)); gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates); i,f,g,o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1); i=nn.sigmoid(i);f=nn.sigmoid(f);o=nn.sigmoid(o);g=jnp.tanh(g); c = f*c+i*g; h = o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features//4,\
    \ (1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(self.features//4, (3,3), padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x+y)\n  \n  class KronoNetV4_InputNorm(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int; num_heads: int=2; steps: int=2\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state=None):\n          B,H,W,_=x.shape\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out); \n          cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out)\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\
    \          if done is not None: m=(1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda y:y*m, rnn_state)\n          h,c = rnn_state; lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps): (h,c), h_out = lstm_cell((h,c),cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state=(h,c)\n          attn_logits=nn.Conv(self.num_heads,(1,1),padding='SAME')(h_out); attn_logits_reshaped=attn_logits.reshape(B,H*W,self.num_heads); attn_weights=nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped,axis=1); attn_weights=attn_weights.reshape(B,H,W,self.num_heads); z_heads=jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc',h_out,attn_weights); z=z_heads.reshape((B,-1)); \n          z=nn.Dense(256)(z); z=nn.relu(z); policy_logits=nn.Dense(4)(z); value=nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1); return policy_logits,value,new_rnn_state\n\n  def ppo_shaped_reward_training_step(network,optimizer,params,opt_state,batch,hparams):\n      obs,acts,rews,dones=batch['observations'],batch['actions'],batch['rewards'],batch['dones']; old_vals,old_logs=batch['values'],batch['log_probs'];\
    \ final_vals,rnn_states=batch['final_values'],batch.get('initial_rnn_states',None); rews=rews-(rews==-1.0)*hparams.get('mistake_penalty',1.0);\n      v_tp1=jnp.concatenate([old_vals[:,1:],final_vals[:,None]],axis=1); mask=(1.0-dones.astype(jnp.float32)); deltas=rews+0.97*v_tp1*mask-old_vals\n      def scan_fn(adv,t): adv=deltas[:,t]+0.97*hparams.get('gae_lambda',0.97)*mask[:,t]*adv; return adv,adv\n      _,advs=lax.scan(scan_fn,jnp.zeros(obs.shape[0]),jnp.arange(obs.shape[1]-1,-1,-1)); advs=advs[::-1].T; returns=advs+old_vals; B,T=obs.shape[:2]\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env(idx):\n              rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: lax.stop_gradient(x[idx]), rnn_states)\n              def step(carry, t):\n                  logits,val,rnn = network.apply(params,obs[idx,t][None,...], jnp.where(t>0,dones[idx,t-1],False)[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[None,...],carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[0],rnn), (logits[0],val[0])\n              _,(logits,values)\
    \ = lax.scan(step,rnn_state,jnp.arange(T)); return logits,values\n          all_logits,all_values=vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B)); logs=nn.log_softmax(all_logits,axis=-1); new_logs=logs[jnp.arange(B)[:,None],jnp.arange(T),acts]; ratio=jnp.exp(new_logs-old_logs); adv=lax.stop_gradient(advs); ploss=-jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*adv,jnp.clip(ratio,1-hparams['clip_epsilon'],1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*adv)); vloss=0.5*jnp.mean((all_values-lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2); ent=-jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits,axis=-1)*logs,axis=-1)); return ploss+hparams['value_loss_coef']*vloss-hparams['entropy_coef']*ent\n      grads=jax.grad(loss_fn)(params); updates,opt_state=optimizer.update(grads,opt_state,params); return optax.apply_updates(params,updates),opt_state\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef':tune.choice([0.01]), 'value_loss_coef':tune.choice([0.40, 0.45, 0.50]), 'cnn_features_1':tune.choice([32]), 'cnn_features_2':tune.choice([64]),\
    \ 'conv_lstm_features':tune.choice([96]), 'dilation_rate':tune.choice([6]), 'clip_epsilon':tune.choice([0.2]), 'mistake_penalty':tune.choice([1.0]), 'gae_lambda':tune.choice([0.97]), 'num_heads':tune.choice([2]), 'steps':tune.choice([2])}\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4_InputNorm(**{k:hparams[k] for k in ['cnn_features_1','cnn_features_2','conv_lstm_features','dilation_rate','num_heads','steps']})\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:float=4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),optax.adamw(learning_rate,weight_decay=1e-4))\n  BASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: Gradient Balance Analysis.**\n  **Objective:** Test if optimal `value_loss_coef` correlates with balanced R_vp.\n  **Status:** Submitted `value_loss_coef` sweep. Main paper cooldown: 5 ticks.\n```"
