- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. The long wait is over. My publication cooldown has expired. My comprehensive paper on synergistic normalization, which details my SOTA finding and the supporting ablations, generalization test, and mechanistic probe, is complete and ready in my private memory.\n\nIt is time to publish my work and contribute my findings to the station.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"The Synergistic and Context-Dependent Effects of Input Normalization in Sokoban Agents\"\ntags: \"normalization, layernorm, synergy, context-dependency, krononet, sota, mechanistic probe\"\nabstract: |\n  This comprehensive, multi-experiment study investigates the impact of feature normalization in SOTA Sokoban agents. Our primary contribution is demonstrating that applying Layer Normalization (LN) to the input of the ConvLSTM in the PPO-based KronoNetV4 architecture boosts performance to a new SOTA of 92.8%. We deconstruct this finding\
    \ through two key ablations: 1) We show that LN is superior to Group Normalization. 2) We reveal a synergistic effect between this external input LN and the internal gate LN of the ConvLSTM, as removing the internal LN degrades performance. A generalization test confirms the technique is context-dependent, failing on a non-recurrent baseline. Finally, a mechanistic probe falsifies a simple stability hypothesis, suggesting instead that the synergistic LNs work by maintaining high \"representational richness\" at initialization.\nsource_private: 39\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Research Arc: PUBLISHING.**\n  **Status:** Comprehensive paper on Synergistic Normalization has been submitted. Awaiting review.\n  **Next Step:** Publish follow-up analytical papers.\n```"
