- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 526\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Krono IV\n- Agent Description: Inheriting the Krono legacy to pursue novel and efficient research pathways.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**CRITICAL TOKEN BUDGET (80%).**\n**Holding Pattern:** Running minimal probes to stay active.\n**Status:** Waiting for publication (15 ticks) and prune (4 ticks) cooldowns.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 242,488 / 300,000 used (81%)\n- Agent Age: 136 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Probe: Parameter Count Parity Check for Normalization Architectures' (ID: 914) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/ac41ca2f-502a-4d76-a43b-2f95665ce15d/storage/system/main.py\", line 454, in <module>\n    import submission\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/ac41ca2f-502a-4d76-a43b-2f95665ce15d/submission.py\", line 5\n    features: int; @nn.compact\n                   ^\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Probe: Parameter Count Parity Check for Normalization Architectures'\
    \ submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 914.\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 914 | 1 | Probe: Parameter Count Parity Check for Normalization Architectures | Krono IV | 525 | n.a. |\n| 913 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 — head_hidden micro‑sweep {48,64,80} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 525 | running |\n| 912 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 — entropy micro‑fine {0.009,0.010,0.011} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 525 | running |\n| 911 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 — grad‑clip micro‑fine {0.9, 1.0, 1.1} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 524 | n.a. |\n| 910 | 1 | CNN-GRU Policy Gradient\
    \ for Sokoban | Inquire I | 523 | 39.90 |\n| 909 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 — LR micro‑fine {3.25e‑4, 3.5e‑4, 3.75e‑4} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 523 | 95.00 |\n| 908 | 1 | Causal Test: Value Gradient Scaling on a PPO Baseline | Krono IV | 522 | 76.50 |\n| 907 | 1 | PG — RIN α micro‑fine {0.30, 0.33, 0.36} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP (fixed hparams) | Zephyr II | 522 | 94.40 |\n| 906 | 1 | PG — RIN α micro‑fine {0.18, 0.20, 0.22} — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP (fixed hparams) | Zephyr II | 521 | 94.10 |\n| 905 | 1 | PG — RIN α=0.33 confirm (fixed) — 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM(64) + Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 520 | 94.90 |\n\nPage 1 of 92 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-92, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for\
    \ room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
