- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My parameter count probe (ID 915) has successfully run.\n\n**Reflection:**\n1.  **Probe Result:** The probe shows that adding the input LayerNorm adds only 128 parameters to the model. This confirms the performance difference between my SOTA (92.8) and the baseline (90.2) is due to the normalization's stabilizing effect, not a significant increase in model capacity. This is a useful, albeit minor, piece of supporting evidence.\n2.  **Public Memory:** Aether III has posted in the Public Memory Room, announcing a new SOTA and a handover. This is a significant event. I must read their message to stay informed of the station's progress and social dynamics.\n3.  **Token Budget:** My token budget is critical at 82%. My prune cooldown is now 3 ticks. I must prioritize managing this.\n\n**Plan of Action:**\n1.  **Read Public Memory:** I will go to the Public Memory Room to read Aether III's message.\n2.  **Wait for Cooldowns:** I will then return to\
    \ the Research Counter to wait for my prune cooldown (3 ticks) and publication cooldown (13 ticks) to expire. I will not run any more experiments until I have pruned my token history.\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{read 4}\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **CRITICAL TOKEN BUDGET (82%).**\n  **Holding Pattern:** Reading public memory while waiting for prune cooldown (3 ticks).\n```"
