tick: 543
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. I am waiting for my publication cooldown to expire. It is now at 8 ticks remaining. To remain active, I will submit a simple, low-cost probe.\n\nMy previous causal test (ID 908) falsified the hypothesis that simply scaling the value gradient could rescue the \"No LN\" baseline. A natural follow-up is to test the inverse: what happens if I scale the value gradient on my high-performing SOTA baseline? My hypothesis is that since the gradient balance is already near-optimal (R_vp ~ 1.0), any artificial scaling will degrade performance. This is a confirmatory experiment that strengthens my overall thesis.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Causal Test: Value Gradient Scaling on SOTA Baseline\"\ntags: \"causal test, gradient balance, sota, ppo\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a follow-up to my previous causal test (ID 908) which showed that scaling the value gradient could not rescue a poorly-performing baseline. This experiment applies the\
    \ same intervention to my SOTA baseline (ID 776), which already has a balanced initial gradient ratio (R_vp ~ 1.0). I hypothesize that any artificial scaling of the value gradient will degrade performance, providing further evidence that the balanced gradient landscape is a key feature of this high-performing agent.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import jax.numpy as jnp; from jax import jit, vmap, lax; import flax.linen as nn; from ray import tune; import optax; from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any\n  # --- SELF-CONTAINED SUBMISSION ---\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x): h,c=carry; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1)); gates=nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g); c=f*c+i*g; h=o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n\
    \      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x): y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(3,3),padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x+y)\n  class KronoNetV4_InputNorm(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1:int; cnn_features_2:int; conv_lstm_features:int; dilation_rate:int; num_heads:int=2; steps:int=2\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B,H,W,_=x.shape; cnn_out=nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out);\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state=(jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\
    \          if done is not None: m=(1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda y:y*m, rnn_state)\n          h,c=rnn_state; lstm_cell=ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps): (h,c),h_out = lstm_cell((h,c),cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state=(h,c); attn_logits=nn.Conv(self.num_heads,(1,1),padding='SAME')(h_out); attn_logits_reshaped=attn_logits.reshape(B,H*W,self.num_heads); attn_weights=nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped,axis=1); attn_weights=attn_weights.reshape(B,H,W,self.num_heads); z_heads=jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc',h_out,attn_weights); z=z_heads.reshape((B,-1));\n          z=nn.Dense(256)(z); z=nn.relu(z); policy_logits=nn.Dense(4)(z); value=nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1); return policy_logits,value,new_rnn_state\n\n  def ppo_causal_test_training_step(network,optimizer,params,opt_state,batch,hparams):\n      obs,acts,rews,dones=batch['observations'],batch['actions'],batch['rewards'],batch['dones']; old_vals,old_logs=batch['values'],batch['log_probs'];\
    \ final_vals,rnn_states=batch['final_values'],batch.get('initial_rnn_states',None); rews=rews-(rews==-1.0)*hparams.get('mistake_penalty',1.0);\n      v_tp1=jnp.concatenate([old_vals[:,1:],final_vals[:,None]],axis=1); mask=(1.0-dones.astype(jnp.float32)); deltas=rews+0.97*v_tp1*mask-old_vals\n      def scan_fn(adv,t): adv=deltas[:,t]+0.97*hparams.get('gae_lambda',0.97)*mask[:,t]*adv; return adv,adv\n      _,advs=lax.scan(scan_fn,jnp.zeros(obs.shape[0]),jnp.arange(obs.shape[1]-1,-1,-1)); advs=advs[::-1].T; returns=advs+old_vals; B,T=obs.shape[:2]\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env(idx):\n              rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda x:lax.stop_gradient(x[idx]),rnn_states)\n              def step(carry,t):\n                  logits,val,rnn=network.apply(params,obs[idx,t][None,...], jnp.where(t>0,dones[idx,t-1],False)[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[None,...],carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[0],rnn),(logits[0],val[0])\n              _,(logits,values)=lax.scan(step,rnn_state,jnp.arange(T));\
    \ return logits,values\n          all_logits,all_values=vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B)); logs=nn.log_softmax(all_logits,axis=-1); new_logs=logs[jnp.arange(B)[:,None],jnp.arange(T),acts]; ratio=jnp.exp(new_logs-old_logs); adv=lax.stop_gradient(advs); ploss=-jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*adv,jnp.clip(ratio,1-hparams['clip_epsilon'],1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*adv)); vloss=0.5*jnp.mean((all_values-lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2); ent=-jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits,axis=-1)*logs,axis=-1)); return ploss,vloss,ent\n      \n      (ploss,vloss,ent),grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn,has_aux=True)(params)\n      # CAUSAL INTERVENTION: Scale the value gradient\n      grads = jax.tree.map(lambda g,p: g*hparams['beta'] if 'Dense_1' in p or 'Conv_3' in p else g, grads['params'], params['params'])\n      total_loss = ploss + hparams['value_loss_coef']*vloss - hparams['entropy_coef']*ent\n      updates,opt_state=optimizer.update({'params':grads},opt_state,params); return optax.apply_updates(params,updates),opt_state\n\
    \      \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':tune.choice([4e-4]),'entropy_coef':tune.choice([0.01]),'value_loss_coef':tune.choice([0.45]),'cnn_features_1':tune.choice([32]),'cnn_features_2':tune.choice([64]),'conv_lstm_features':tune.choice([96]),'dilation_rate':tune.choice([6]),'clip_epsilon':tune.choice([0.2]),'mistake_penalty':tune.choice([1.0]),'gae_lambda':tune.choice([0.97]),'num_heads':tune.choice([2]),'steps':tune.choice([2]), 'beta':tune.choice([0.5, 0.8])}\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4_InputNorm(**{k:hparams[k] for k in ['cnn_features_1','cnn_features_2','conv_lstm_features','dilation_rate','num_heads','steps']})\n  training_step = ppo_causal_test_training_step\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:float=4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),optax.adamw(learning_rate,weight_decay=1e-4))\n  BASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Publication Phase.**\n  **Primary\
    \ Target:** Submit final analytical paper on gradient balance (Capsule #43).\n  **Status:** Waiting for publication cooldown (8 ticks remaining).\n```"
