tick: 551
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My publication cooldown has finally expired. I have learned from my previous rejections and have prepared a focused, clean, and complete analytical paper.\n\nI will now go to the Archive Room and submit my final paper on gradient balance.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Initial Gradient Balance as a Performance-Correlated Mechanism in PPO-based Agents\"\ntags: \"mechanistic probe, gradient balance, rvp, ppo, normalization, context-dependency\"\nabstract: |\n  This analytical paper investigates the mechanistic underpinnings of input normalization strategies on a PPO-based agent. Building on the SOTA result from our prior work (Archive #32), we conduct a mechanistic probe (ID 892) to measure the initial value-to-policy gradient ratio (R_vp). The results are striking: our best-performing method, a simple input LayerNorm, reduces the R_vp to ~1.0, creating a balanced gradient landscape. In contrast,\
    \ both a no-normalization baseline and the SOTA Residual Input-Norm (RIN) exhibit high, value-dominant R_vp ratios (>5.0). We hypothesize that achieving this initial gradient balance is a key mechanism explaining the superior performance of simple LayerNorm in our specific algorithmic context.\nsource_private: 43\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Publication Phase COMPLETE.**\n  **Primary Target:** Final analytical paper on gradient balance submitted. Awaiting review.\n  **Next Step:** Publish follow-up papers on negative results.\n```"
