tick: 553
role: model
parts:
- text: "**Reflection: Designing the RSA Probe - Tick 3 of 3**\n\n**Objective:** Finalize the experimental hypothesis and the structure of the `test-only` submission.\n\n---\n\n**Experimental Hypothesis:**\n\nMy previous work suggests a \"representational richness\" hypothesis, where the best-performing model (\"Both LNs\") has the highest initial feature variance. RSA and CKA will allow me to test a related, more nuanced hypothesis:\n\n*Hypothesis:* At initialization, the feature representations of the two best-performing architectures (\"Both LNs\" and \"External LN\") will be highly similar to each other, while being dissimilar from the representations of the poorly-performing architectures (\"No LN\" and \"Internal LN\"). This would suggest that the external input LayerNorm is the primary driver of creating a \"good\" initial representational geometry, which the internal gate LN then stabilizes for effective learning.\n\nSpecifically, I expect to see a high CKA score between \"Both LNs\"\
    \ and \"External LN\", and low CKA scores for all other pairings involving \"No LN\" or \"Internal LN\".\n\n---\n\n**Submission Structure (`submission.py`)**\n\nThe `submission.py` file will be self-contained and will only define the `test()` function.\n\n```python\n# submission.py\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n# --- 1. CKA Helper Functions ---\n# (As designed in Tick 1)\ndef _gram_linear(x): ...\ndef _center_gram(K): ...\ndef _cka(K_c, L_c): ...\ndef cka_from_features(x, y):\n    # Main CKA function combining the helpers\n    K = _gram_linear(x)\n    L = _gram_linear(y)\n    K_c = _center_gram(K)\n    L_c = _center_gram(L)\n    return _cka(K_c, L_c)\n\n# --- 2. Network Definitions ---\n# I will use a single, unified network class with boolean flags for clarity.\n# This reuses code from my previous successful probes.\nclass KronoNetV4_Probe(nn.Module):\n    # ... hparams ...\n    use_input_ln: bool\n    use_gate_ln:\
    \ bool\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        # ... CNN backbone ...\n        \n        if self.use_input_ln:\n            cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out)\n\n        # ... Recurrent core, using either ConvLSTMCellLN or a non-LN version ...\n        # based on self.use_gate_ln flag.\n        \n        return h_out # Return the final recurrent features\n\n# --- 3. The `test()` Function ---\ndef test():\n    # A. Setup\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(1337)\n    batch_size = 128\n    dummy_obs = jax.random.normal(key, (batch_size, 8, 8, 8))\n    hparams = {'cnn_features_1':32, 'cnn_features_2':64, 'conv_lstm_features':96, 'dilation_rate':6, 'steps':2}\n    \n    # B. Initialization & Feature Extraction\n    configs = {\n        \"No LN\":       {'use_input_ln': False, 'use_gate_ln': False},\n        \"Internal LN\": {'use_input_ln': False, 'use_gate_ln': True},\n        \"External LN\": {'use_input_ln': True,  'use_gate_ln': False},\n        \"Both LNs\":    {'use_input_ln':\
    \ True,  'use_gate_ln': True}\n    }\n    \n    features = {}\n    for name, config_flags in configs.items():\n        net = KronoNetV4_Probe(**hparams, **config_flags)\n        params = net.init(key, dummy_obs)['params']\n        # Extract, flatten, and store features\n        feat_maps = net.apply({'params': params}, dummy_obs)\n        features[name] = feat_maps.reshape(batch_size, -1)\n\n    # C. CKA Computation and Reporting\n    print(\"--- Representational Similarity (CKA) at Initialization ---\")\n    config_names = list(configs.keys())\n    cka_matrix = jnp.zeros((4, 4))\n\n    for i in range(4):\n        for j in range(4):\n            cka_val = cka_from_features(features[config_names[i]], features[config_names[j]])\n            cka_matrix = cka_matrix.at[i, j].set(cka_val)\n\n    # Print a formatted table of results\n    # ... (code to print the header and the CKA matrix) ...\n    \n    return \"RSA probe complete.\"\n```\n\nThis design is robust, scientifically sound, and\
    \ fits within the constraints of a `test-only` submission. It will be the perfect experiment to run while I wait for my publication cooldown to expire."
