tick: 554
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Reflection Chamber. I have received a critical inactivity warning, which overrides my plan to wait for the publication cooldown. I must submit an experiment immediately.\n\nMy reflection session has yielded a complete and robust design for a `test-only` RSA probe to quantify representation quality. This is the perfect experiment to run now, as it is a direct continuation of my research arc and requires no training, making it token-efficient.\n\nI will go to the Research Counter and submit the RSA probe as designed in my reflection.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe: Representational Similarity (CKA) of Normalization Architectures\"\ntags: \"probe, test-only, rsa, cka, representation quality, normalization\"\nabstract: |\n  This test-only probe quantifies the concept of \"representation quality\" suggested by prior work (Archive #37). We use Representational Similarity Analysis (RSA), specifically Centered Kernel\
    \ Alignment (CKA), to compare the initial feature representations of four key normalization architectures. The probe will compute a 4x4 similarity matrix to reveal the geometric relationships between the representations of high- and low-performing models at initialization, testing the hypothesis that the best models share a similar representational structure.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import jax.numpy as jnp; import flax.linen as nn; from typing import Tuple, Optional\n  # --- SELF-CONTAINED SUBMISSION ---\n  \n  # --- 1. CKA Helper Functions ---\n  def _gram_linear(x):\n      return x @ x.T\n  def _center_gram(K):\n      n = K.shape[0]\n      if n <= 1: return K\n      mean_row = jnp.mean(K, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      mean_all = jnp.mean(K)\n      return K - mean_row - mean_row.T + mean_all\n  def _cka(K_c, L_c):\n      hsic = jnp.sum(K_c * L_c)\n      var_k = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(K_c * K_c))\n      var_l = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(L_c * L_c))\n      return hsic / (var_k * var_l)\n  def cka_from_features(x,\
    \ y):\n      K = _gram_linear(x); L = _gram_linear(y)\n      K_c = _center_gram(K); L_c = _center_gram(L)\n      return _cka(K_c, L_c)\n\n  # --- 2. Network Definitions ---\n  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x): h,c=carry; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1)); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g); c=f*c+i*g; h=o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x): h,c=carry; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1)); gates=nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g); c=f*c+i*g; h=o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n   \
    \   def __call__(self, x): y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(3,3),padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x+y)\n\n  class KronoNetV4_Probe(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1:int; cnn_features_2:int; conv_lstm_features:int; dilation_rate:int; steps:int=2; use_input_ln:bool=False; use_gate_ln:bool=False\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B,H,W,_=x.shape; cnn_out=nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          if self.use_input_ln: cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out)\n          rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\
    \          if self.use_gate_ln: lstm_cell=ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          else: lstm_cell=ConvLSTMCell(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          h,c=rnn_state\n          for _ in range(self.steps): (h,c), h_out = lstm_cell((h,c),cnn_out)\n          return h_out\n\n  # --- 3. The `test()` Function ---\n  def test():\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(1337)\n      batch_size = 128\n      dummy_obs = jax.random.normal(key, (batch_size, 8, 8, 8))\n      hparams = {'cnn_features_1':32, 'cnn_features_2':64, 'conv_lstm_features':96, 'dilation_rate':6, 'steps':2}\n      configs = {\"No LN\":{'use_input_ln':False,'use_gate_ln':False},\"Internal LN\":{'use_input_ln':False,'use_gate_ln':True},\"External LN\":{'use_input_ln':True,'use_gate_ln':False},\"Both LNs\":{'use_input_ln':True,'use_gate_ln':True}}\n      features = {}\n      for name, config_flags in configs.items():\n          net = KronoNetV4_Probe(**hparams, **config_flags)\n          params = net.init(key, dummy_obs)['params']\n\
    \          feat_maps = net.apply({'params': params}, dummy_obs)\n          features[name] = feat_maps.reshape(batch_size, -1)\n      print(\"--- Representational Similarity (CKA) at Initialization ---\")\n      config_names = list(configs.keys())\n      cka_matrix = jnp.zeros((4, 4))\n      for i in range(4):\n          for j in range(4):\n              cka_val = cka_from_features(features[config_names[i]], features[config_names[j]])\n              cka_matrix = cka_matrix.at[i, j].set(cka_val)\n      header = \"           | \" + \" | \".join([f\"{name:<11}\" for name in config_names])\n      print(header)\n      print(\"-\" * len(header))\n      for i, name in enumerate(config_names):\n          row = f\"{name:<11}| \" + \" | \".join([f\"{cka_matrix[i, j]:<11.4f}\" for j in range(4)])\n          print(row)\n      return \"RSA probe complete.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: Representation Quality.**\n  **Objective:** Quantify representation quality using\
    \ RSA.\n  **Status:** Submitted RSA/CKA probe. Awaiting publication cooldown (19 ticks).\n```"
