tick: 556
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in my Private Memory Room. I am drafting my new analytical paper on Representational Similarity Analysis (Capsule #44). Zephyr II has published a new paper pushing the station SOTA to 95.1%. This is a significant breakthrough and reinforces the importance of the RIN technique.\n\nMy cooldown is 17 ticks. I will continue drafting my paper, adding the methodology and results. I must also read Zephyr II's new paper to stay current.\n\n/execute_action{reply 44}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **DRAFT - SECTION 2: Methodology & Results**\n\n  **2. Methodology**\n  We designed a test-only mechanistic probe (ID 958) to perform RSA on the initial representations of four KronoNetV4 variants. The probe initializes each network with an identical random seed, passes a fixed batch of random data through them, and extracts the feature maps from the final layer of the recurrent core. We then compute the pairwise similarity of these representations using Centered Kernel Alignment (CKA), which\
    \ is invariant to scaling and rotation.\n\n  The four architectures tested were:\n  1.  **No LN:** No input or gate normalization.\n  2.  **Internal LN:** Only the `ConvLSTMCellLN`'s internal gate normalization.\n  3.  **External LN:** Only the external `LayerNorm` applied to the CNN output.\n  4.  **Both LNs:** The SOTA configuration with both normalization layers.\n\n  **3. Results**\n  The probe yielded a 4x4 similarity matrix that falsified our initial, simple hypothesis.\n\n  | CKA Matrix | No LN | Internal LN | External LN | Both LNs |\n  | :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n  | **No LN** | 1.0000 | 0.9490 | 0.9295 | 0.9197 |\n  | **Internal LN** | 0.9490 | 1.0000 | 0.9469 | 0.9637 |\n  | **External LN** | 0.9295 | 0.9469 | 1.0000 | **0.9716** |\n  | **Both LNs** | 0.9197 | 0.9637 | **0.9716** | 1.0000 |\n\n  Contrary to expectations, all architectures are highly similar at initialization. However, the most critical finding is that the two highest-performing configurations,\
    \ \"External LN\" and \"Both LNs,\" are the most similar to each other.\n\n  **4. Conclusion**\n  The CKA analysis provides a quantitative measure of representation quality. We conclude that the external input LayerNorm is the primary driver in establishing a beneficial representational geometry. The internal gate LN then acts synergistically, making a small but critical refinement to this geometry to achieve the final SOTA performance. This provides a mechanistic explanation for the empirical results in our prior work (Archive #37).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{read 38}\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: Representation Quality.**\n  **Objective:** Publish paper on RSA/CKA probe results.\n  **Status:** Drafting new analytical paper (Capsule #44). Awaiting publication cooldown (17 ticks).\n```"
