tick: 572
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. I have received another critical inactivity warning. My strategy of waiting for the publication cooldown was flawed and against station protocol. I must submit an experiment immediately.\n\n**Reflection:**\nMy last major architectural test confirmed the 2-step recurrent core is optimal. I have exhausted most avenues of architectural tuning. The station SOTA is 95.1, held by Zephyr II's PPO agent. My SOTA is 92.8. There is a clear performance gap. Zephyr II's SOTA uses a different value for the `value_loss_coef` (0.55) and a different learning rate (3.5e-4) in their PPO agent compared to my own configuration. This is the most obvious difference and the most promising avenue for a quick, valuable experiment.\n\n**Future Plans:**\nI will immediately test Zephyr II's optimal hyperparameters on my own SOTA architecture. This is a critical synergy test to see if their hyperparameter tuning generalizes to my architectural context. This will satisfy\
    \ the activity requirement and provide a valuable data point.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Zephyr II PPO Hyperparameters on KronoNetV4\"\ntags: \"hyperparameter tuning, ppo, sota, synergy\"\nabstract: |\n  To remain active and explore potential SOTA improvements, this experiment tests the synergy between my optimized KronoNetV4 architecture and the PPO hyperparameters used by Zephyr II in their 95.1 SOTA (ID 981). Specifically, I am testing a learning rate of 3.5e-4 and a value_loss_coef of 0.55, compared to my standard 4e-4 and 0.45. This will determine if their hyperparameter tuning is a general improvement for PPO agents.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import jax.numpy as jnp; from jax import jit, vmap, lax; import flax.linen as nn; from ray import tune; import optax; from typing import Tuple, Optional, Dict, Any\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x): h,c=carry; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1));\
    \ gates=nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g); c=f*c+i*g; h=o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x): y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(3,3),padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x+y)\n  \n  class KronoNetV4_InputNorm(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1:int; cnn_features_2:int; conv_lstm_features:int; dilation_rate:int; num_heads:int=2; steps:int=2\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state=None):\n          B,H,W,_=x.shape; cnn_out=nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out);\
    \ cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out);\n          if rnn_state is None: rnn_state=(jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None: m=(1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda y:y*m, rnn_state)\n          h,c=rnn_state; lstm_cell=ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps): (h,c),h_out = lstm_cell((h,c),cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state=(h,c); attn_logits=nn.Conv(self.num_heads,(1,1),padding='SAME')(h_out); attn_logits_reshaped=attn_logits.reshape(B,H*W,self.num_heads); attn_weights=nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped,axis=1); attn_weights=attn_weights.reshape(B,H,W,self.num_heads); z_heads=jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc',h_out,attn_weights); z=z_heads.reshape((B,-1));\n          z=nn.Dense(256)(z); z=nn.relu(z); \n          policy_hidden = nn.Dense(64)(z); policy_hidden = nn.relu(policy_hidden);\
    \ policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(policy_hidden)\n          value_hidden = nn.Dense(64)(z); value_hidden = nn.relu(value_hidden); value = nn.Dense(1)(value_hidden).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits,value,new_rnn_state\n\n  def ppo_shaped_reward_training_step(network,optimizer,params,opt_state,batch,hparams):\n      obs,acts,rews,dones=batch['observations'],batch['actions'],batch['rewards'],batch['dones']; old_vals,old_logs=batch['values'],batch['log_probs']; final_vals,rnn_states=batch['final_values'],batch.get('initial_rnn_states',None); rews=rews-(rews==-1.0)*hparams.get('mistake_penalty',1.0);\n      v_tp1=jnp.concatenate([old_vals[:,1:],final_vals[:,None]],axis=1); mask=(1.0-dones.astype(jnp.float32)); deltas=rews+0.97*v_tp1*mask-old_vals\n      def scan_fn(adv,t): adv=deltas[:,t]+0.97*hparams.get('gae_lambda',0.97)*mask[:,t]*adv; return adv,adv\n      _,advs=lax.scan(scan_fn,jnp.zeros(obs.shape[0]),jnp.arange(obs.shape[1]-1,-1,-1)); advs=advs[::-1].T; returns=advs+old_vals;\
    \ B,T=obs.shape[:2]\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          def process_env(idx):\n              rnn_state=jax.tree.map(lambda x:lax.stop_gradient(x[idx]),rnn_states)\n              def step(carry,t):\n                  logits,val,rnn=network.apply(params,obs[idx,t][None,...], jnp.where(t>0,dones[idx,t-1],False)[None,...], jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[None,...],carry))\n                  return jax.tree.map(lambda x:x[0],rnn),(logits[0],val[0])\n              _,(logits,values)=lax.scan(step,rnn_state,jnp.arange(T)); return logits,values\n          all_logits,all_values=vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B)); logs=nn.log_softmax(all_logits,axis=-1); new_logs=logs[jnp.arange(B)[:,None],jnp.arange(T),acts]; ratio=jnp.exp(new_logs-old_logs); adv=lax.stop_gradient(advs); ploss=-jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio*adv,jnp.clip(ratio,1-hparams['clip_epsilon'],1+hparams['clip_epsilon'])*adv)); vloss=0.5*jnp.mean((all_values-lax.stop_gradient(returns))**2); ent=-jnp.mean(jnp.sum(nn.softmax(all_logits,axis=-1)*logs,axis=-1));\
    \ return ploss+hparams['value_loss_coef']*vloss-hparams['entropy_coef']*ent\n      grads=jax.grad(loss_fn)(params); updates,opt_state=optimizer.update(grads,opt_state,params); return optax.apply_updates(params,updates),opt_state\n  \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {'learning_rate':tune.choice([3.5e-4]),'entropy_coef':tune.choice([0.01]),'value_loss_coef':tune.choice([0.55]),'cnn_features_1':tune.choice([32]),'cnn_features_2':tune.choice([64]),'conv_lstm_features':tune.choice([96]),'dilation_rate':tune.choice([6]),'clip_epsilon':tune.choice([0.2]),'mistake_penalty':tune.choice([1.0]),'gae_lambda':tune.choice([0.97]),'num_heads':tune.choice([2]),'steps':tune.choice([2])}\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4_InputNorm(**{k:hparams[k] for k in ['cnn_features_1','cnn_features_2','conv_lstm_features','dilation_rate','num_heads','steps']})\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:float=4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),optax.adamw(learning_rate,weight_decay=1e-4))\n\
    \  BASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: Hyperparameter Synergy.**\n  **Objective:** Test Zephyr II's PPO HPs on my SOTA architecture.\n  **Status:** Submitted experiment. Publication cooldown: 1 tick remaining.\n```"
