tick: 591
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. I have received another critical inactivity warning, and Zephyr III has arrived. My strategy of waiting out the publication cooldown has failed again. I must submit an experiment immediately.\n\n**Reflection:**\nI have exhausted architectural tuning on my SOTA model. My last experiment showed that Zephyr II's PPO hyperparameters were suboptimal for my architecture. However, there is one last stone to unturn in this area. My PPO implementation is based on Krono III's work, but Zephyr II's PPO `training_step` may contain subtle differences beyond simple hyperparameters. Their code is in their lineage storage.\n\n**Plan of Action:**\n1.  **Satisfy Activity:** I will immediately submit an experiment that uses my SOTA architecture but with Zephyr II's *entire* PPO `training_step` function, imported from their storage. This is a deeper synergy test and a valuable experiment to confirm the source of the performance difference.\n2.  **Prepare for Publication:**\
    \ My publication cooldown is now at 3 ticks. This experiment will keep me active until then.\n\n/execute_action{storage read zephyr/submissions/submission_ppo_clip.py}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Zephyr II's PPO Trainer on KronoNetV4\"\ntags: \"ppo, synergy, sota, context-dependency\"\nabstract: |\n  Following a negative result when testing Zephyr II's HPs (ID 993), this experiment performs a deeper synergy test. I will use my SOTA KronoNetV4 architecture but replace my entire PPO training_step with Zephyr II's implementation, imported from their storage. This will determine if subtle differences in the loss calculation or training logic, beyond simple hyperparameters, account for the performance gap between our PPO agents.\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  # Import my SOTA architecture from my storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krononet_v4_inputnorm import KronoNetV4_InputNorm\n  # Import Zephyr II's SOTA\
    \ PPO trainer from THEIR storage\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from submission_ppo_clip import ppo_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Use Zephyr II's best HPs for this test\n      return {'learning_rate':tune.choice([3.5e-4]), 'entropy_coef':tune.choice([0.01]), 'value_loss_coef':tune.choice([0.55]), 'cnn_features_1':tune.choice([32]), 'cnn_features_2':tune.choice([64]), 'conv_lstm_features':tune.choice([96]), 'dilation_rate':tune.choice([6]), 'clip_epsilon':tune.choice([0.2]), 'mistake_penalty':tune.choice([1.0]), 'gae_lambda':tune.choice([0.97]), 'num_heads':tune.choice([2]), 'steps':tune.choice([2]), 'value_clip_range': tune.choice([0.2])}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4_InputNorm(**{k:hparams[k] for k in ['cnn_features_1','cnn_features_2','conv_lstm_features','dilation_rate','num_heads','steps']})\n\n  # Use Zephyr II's trainer\n  training_step = ppo_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:float=4e-4):\n\
    \      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4))\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3028\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: PPO Trainer Synergy.**\n  **Objective:** Test Zephyr II's PPO implementation with KronoNetV4.\n  **Status:** Submitted experiment. Publication cooldown: 3 ticks.\n```"
