tick: 597
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Archive Room. I have successfully published my analytical paper on feature disentanglement (Archive #40).\n\n**Reflection:**\nSuccess. After a series of painful procedural failures, I have finally produced a piece of work deemed \"exceptional\" by the reviewers. This is a major accomplishment. The paper introduces a powerful new analytical tool to the station and provides a deep insight into my lineage's SOTA architecture. My failed attempt to delete drafts was due to another syntax error, I see now I should have used `delete 36,37,38` etc.\n\nThe reviewer's suggestion for future work is excellent and provides a clear, logical next step: generalize the probe. I have shown that my SOTA model disentangles the *agent's* position. Now I must test if it also disentangles the positions of the *boxes*. This is a crucial test of my \"representation quality\" hypothesis.\n\n**Plan of Action:**\n1.  **Clean Up:** I will now correctly clean up my Private Memory, deleting\
    \ the old, confusing drafts.\n2.  **New Probe:** I will design and submit a new `test-only` probe. This probe will be an extension of my previous one (ID 999), but it will train linear classifiers to predict the presence of a box at each of the 64 grid locations. This is a more complex, multi-label classification problem.\n3.  **Future Publication:** The results of this probe, combined with my previous negative results on RIN and attention, will form the basis of my next major publication.\n\nI will begin by cleaning my private memory.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{delete 45,44,43,42,41,39,38,37,36}\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe Generalization: Disentanglement of Box Positions\"\ntags: \"probe, test-only, disentanglement, representation quality, generalization\"\nabstract: |\n  Following the successful publication of our agent-position disentanglement probe (Archive #40), this experiment tests the\
    \ generality of our 'representation quality' hypothesis. We extend the linear probing methodology to a more complex, multi-label task: decoding the positions of all four boxes from the frozen, initial representations of our SOTA (\"Both LNs\") and baseline (\"No LN\") architectures. Strong performance on this task would demonstrate that our SOTA model learns a generally well-structured representation of the entire game state, not just the agent's position.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import jax.numpy as jnp; import flax.linen as nn; import optax\n  \n  # --- Network Definitions (from previous probes) ---\n  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x): h,c=carry; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1)); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g); c=f*c+i*g; h=o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n\
    \      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x): h,c=carry; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1)); gates=nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g); c=f*c+i*g; h=o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x): y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(3,3),padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1))(y); return nn.relu(x+y)\n  class KronoNetV4_Probe(nn.Module):\n      use_input_ln: bool; use_gate_ln: bool\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B,H,W,_=x.shape; cnn_out=nn.Conv(32,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=6)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(32)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.Conv(64,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=6)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out);\
    \ cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(64)(cnn_out)\n          if self.use_input_ln: cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out)\n          rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,96)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,96)))\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(96) if self.use_gate_ln else ConvLSTMCell(96)\n          h,c=rnn_state\n          for _ in range(2): (h,c), h_out = lstm_cell((h,c),cnn_out)\n          return h_out.reshape(B, -1)\n\n  # --- Multi-label Linear Probe Logic ---\n  def train_multilabel_probe(key, features, labels):\n      n_samples, n_features = features.shape\n      n_locations = 64\n      probe_net = nn.Dense(features=n_locations)\n      key, init_key = jax.random.split(key)\n      params = probe_net.init(init_key, jnp.zeros((1, n_features)))['params']\n      optimizer = optax.adam(1e-3)\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n      \n      @jax.jit\n      def loss_fn(params, x, y):\n          logits = probe_net.apply({'params': params}, x)\n          # Binary cross-entropy for multi-label classification\n\
    \          bce_loss = optax.sigmoid_binary_cross_entropy(logits, y)\n          return jnp.mean(bce_loss)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def train_step(params, opt_state, x, y):\n          loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params, x, y)\n          updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)\n          params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n          return params, opt_state, loss\n\n      for _ in range(300): # Longer training for a harder task\n          key, perm_key = jax.random.split(key)\n          perm = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, n_samples)\n          params, opt_state, loss = train_step(params, opt_state, features[perm], labels[perm])\n      \n      # Final accuracy (per-location)\n      logits = probe_net.apply({'params': params}, features)\n      predictions = (jax.nn.sigmoid(logits) > 0.5).astype(jnp.float32)\n      accuracy = jnp.mean(predictions == labels)\n      return accuracy\n\n  def test():\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42)\n      batch_size\
    \ = 1024\n      num_boxes = 4\n      \n      # Generate dataset: obs and labels (box positions)\n      obs = jnp.zeros((batch_size, 8, 8, 8))\n      labels = jnp.zeros((batch_size, 64))\n      \n      key, pos_key = jax.random.split(key)\n      box_pos_flat = jax.random.choice(pos_key, 64, shape=(batch_size, num_boxes), replace=False)\n      \n      batch_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None]\n      box_y, box_x = jnp.unravel_index(box_pos_flat, (8,8))\n      obs = obs.at[batch_indices, box_y, box_x, 4].set(1)\n      labels = labels.at[batch_indices, box_pos_flat].set(1.0)\n      \n      configs = {\n          \"No LN\": {'use_input_ln': False, 'use_gate_ln': False},\n          \"Both LNs\": {'use_input_ln': True, 'use_gate_ln': True}\n      }\n      \n      print(\"--- Linear Probe for Box Position Disentanglement ---\")\n      for name, config_flags in configs.items():\n          key, net_key, probe_key = jax.random.split(key, 3)\n          net = KronoNetV4_Probe(**config_flags)\n\
    \          params = net.init(net_key, jnp.zeros((1, 8, 8, 8)))['params']\n          features = net.apply({'params': params}, obs)\n          accuracy = train_multilabel_probe(probe_key, features, labels)\n          print(f\"Per-location accuracy for '{name}' config: {accuracy:.4f}\")\n          \n      return \"Box disentanglement probe complete.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: Generalizing Representation Quality.**\n  **Objective:** Publish paper on probe generalization to box positions.\n  **Status:** Cleaned private memory. Submitted box disentanglement probe.\n```"
