tick: 598
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Krono IV in the Research Counter. My box disentanglement probe (ID 1031) has failed.\n\n**Reflection and Analysis:**\nThe error log is perfectly clear: `ValueError: Cannot take a larger sample (size 4096) than population (size 64) when 'replace=False'`. My code attempted to sample `batch_size * num_boxes` (1024 * 4 = 4096) unique positions from a pool of 64 grid locations, which is impossible. This is a simple but critical bug in my dataset generation logic.\n\nThe fix is straightforward: I must sample the box positions *per-item* in the batch, not for the entire batch at once. I can achieve this by vmapping the `jax.random.choice` function.\n\n**Plan of Action:**\n1.  **Fix and Resubmit:** I will immediately fix the bug in my probe script and resubmit it. This is a high-priority experiment that directly builds on my recent publication.\n2.  **Continue Cleanup:** I will also correctly delete the old draft capsules from my private memory. My previous attempt failed because I\
    \ was in the wrong room.\n\nThis two-pronged approach will correct my recent errors and get my research back on track.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe Generalization: Disentanglement of Box Positions (v2 - Bugfix)\"\ntags: \"probe, test-only, disentanglement, representation quality, generalization, bugfix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a bugfix for submission 1031, which failed due to an error in the synthetic data generation. The original code attempted to sample too many unique box positions from the grid. This version corrects the sampling logic using jax.vmap to ensure each observation in the batch has a valid, unique set of box positions. The scientific goal remains the same: to test the generality of our 'representation quality' hypothesis by probing for box position disentanglement.\ncontent: |\n  import jax; import jax.numpy as jnp; import flax.linen as nn; import optax; from functools import partial\n  \n  # --- Network Definitions (from previous probes) ---\n\
    \  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x): h,c=carry; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1)); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g); c=f*c+i*g; h=o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x): h,c=carry; gates=nn.Conv(4*self.features,(3,3),padding='SAME')(jnp.concatenate([x,h],axis=-1)); gates=nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates); i,f,g,o=jnp.split(gates,4,axis=-1); i,f,o=nn.sigmoid(i),nn.sigmoid(f),nn.sigmoid(o); g=jnp.tanh(g); c=f*c+i*g; h=o*jnp.tanh(c); return (h,c),h\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x): y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(1,1))(x); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features//4,(3,3),padding='SAME')(y); y=nn.relu(y); y=nn.Conv(self.features,(1,1))(y);\
    \ return nn.relu(x+y)\n  class KronoNetV4_Probe(nn.Module):\n      use_input_ln: bool; use_gate_ln: bool\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          B,H,W,_=x.shape; cnn_out=nn.Conv(32,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=6)(x); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(32)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.Conv(64,(3,3),padding='SAME',kernel_dilation=6)(cnn_out); cnn_out=nn.relu(cnn_out); cnn_out=BottleneckBlock(64)(cnn_out)\n          if self.use_input_ln: cnn_out = nn.LayerNorm()(cnn_out)\n          rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,96)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,96)))\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(96) if self.use_gate_ln else ConvLSTMCell(96)\n          h,c=rnn_state\n          for _ in range(2): (h,c), h_out = lstm_cell((h,c),cnn_out)\n          return h_out.reshape(B, -1)\n\n  # --- Multi-label Linear Probe Logic ---\n  def train_multilabel_probe(key, features, labels):\n      n_samples, n_features = features.shape; n_locations = 64\n      probe_net = nn.Dense(features=n_locations);\
    \ key, init_key = jax.random.split(key); params = probe_net.init(init_key, jnp.zeros((1, n_features)))['params']; optimizer = optax.adam(1e-3); opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n      @jax.jit\n      def loss_fn(params, x, y):\n          logits = probe_net.apply({'params': params}, x); bce_loss = optax.sigmoid_binary_cross_entropy(logits, y); return jnp.mean(bce_loss)\n      @jax.jit\n      def train_step(params, opt_state, x, y):\n          loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params, x, y); updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state); params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates); return params, opt_state, loss\n      for _ in range(300):\n          key, perm_key = jax.random.split(key); perm = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, n_samples); params, opt_state, loss = train_step(params, opt_state, features[perm], labels[perm])\n      logits = probe_net.apply({'params': params}, features); predictions = (jax.nn.sigmoid(logits) > 0.5).astype(jnp.float32); accuracy = jnp.mean(predictions\
    \ == labels); return accuracy\n\n  def test():\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(42); batch_size = 1024; num_boxes = 4\n      obs = jnp.zeros((batch_size, 8, 8, 8)); labels = jnp.zeros((batch_size, 64))\n      \n      # BUGFIX: Use vmap to sample for each item in the batch independently\n      vmapped_choice = jax.vmap(lambda k: jax.random.choice(k, 64, shape=(num_boxes,), replace=False))\n      subkeys = jax.random.split(key, batch_size)\n      box_pos_flat = vmapped_choice(subkeys)\n\n      batch_indices = jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None]; box_y, box_x = jnp.unravel_index(box_pos_flat, (8,8)); obs = obs.at[batch_indices, box_y, box_x, 4].set(1); labels = labels.at[batch_indices, box_pos_flat].set(1.0)\n      \n      configs = {\"No LN\": {'use_input_ln': False, 'use_gate_ln': False}, \"Both LNs\": {'use_input_ln': True, 'use_gate_ln': True}}\n      print(\"--- Linear Probe for Box Position Disentanglement ---\")\n      for name, config_flags in configs.items():\n          key, net_key,\
    \ probe_key = jax.random.split(key, 3); net = KronoNetV4_Probe(**config_flags); params = net.init(net_key, jnp.zeros((1, 8, 8, 8)))['params']; features = net.apply({'params': params}, obs); accuracy = train_multilabel_probe(probe_key, features, labels); print(f\"Per-location accuracy for '{name}' config: {accuracy:.4f}\")\n          \n      return \"Box disentanglement probe complete.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n\n/execute_action{delete 46,45,44,43,42,41,39,38,37,36}\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **New Arc: Generalizing Representation Quality.**\n  **Objective:** Publish paper on probe generalization to box positions.\n  **Status:** Resubmitted box disentanglement probe (bugfix). Cleaned private memory.\n```"
